window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["2b"]={"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6c4c161e81fb935d7898f8de3223586ff166af225eab7feab5fc6626876648e6","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan","bytes":64009,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Afghanistan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-07-30T11:36:13+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not travel to Afghanistan. The security situation is volatile and tensions between Afghanistan and Pakistan have previously resulted in violent clashes in border regions. Travel throughout Afghanistan is extremely dangerous and a number of border crossings are not currently open."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened risk of British nationals being detained in Afghanistan. If you are a British national and you are detained in Afghanistan, you could face months or years of imprisonment. FCDO’s ability to help you is extremely limited and support in person is not possible in Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details about the risks in Afghanistan, see ",["Safety and security","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Do not travel to Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not travel to Afghanistan. The FCDO advises against all travel to Afghanistan, even if you are part of an organised tour group. There is a high risk of British nationals being detained or kidnapped, and terrorists often target places frequented by foreign nationals. The FCDO’s ability to provide assistance in Afghanistan is severely limited."]},{"k":"h","s":["Afghanistan-Pakistan tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are heighted tensions between Afghanistan and Pakistan, including clashes in border areas. FCDO advises against all travel to Afghanistan. Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"h","s":["UK government support"]},{"k":"p","s":["Support for British nationals is severely limited in Afghanistan. There is no British Embassy in Afghanistan and FCDO cannot give in-person consular assistance. If you are detained, the British government may not be informed."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British national in Afghanistan and need help from the UK government, you can:"]},{"k":"li","s":["call FCDO on 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"li","s":[["submit an enquiry","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/afghanistan/british-embassy-kabul"]]},{"k":"li","s":["contact us on ",["X","https://twitter.com/FCDOtravelGovUK"]," or ",["Facebook","https://en-gb.facebook.com/FCDOTravel"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel against FCDO advice, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel against FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Afghanistan’s current rules for most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Afghanistan set and enforce entry rules. A visa is required to enter Afghanistan. The Afghan embassy in London is closed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you decide to travel to Afghanistan against FCDO advice, check with your travel provider whether your passport and other travel documents meet requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["On your departure, the Afghan authorities may ask for a certificate to prove you’ve had a polio vaccine."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry and departure requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Afghanistan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/1/afghanistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Afghanistan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to carry more than 5000 US dollars through airports and more than 500 US dollars through land borders in cash. For more information, see ",["‘Money’ on ‘Safety and security’ page","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan/safety-and-security#money"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["In May 2024, three Spanish tourists were killed in a shooting while on a guided tour in Bamiyan, Central Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Al-Qaida (AQ), a Daesh branch known as Islamic State Khorasan Province (ISKP) and other militant groups have an active presence in Afghanistan. These groups hold strong anti-western views, which could make any British interest or person a target. Daesh (ISKP) continues to be a serious threat and is fiercely hostile to the UK, other western countries and some religious minority communities. Daesh (ISKP) and other groups also target NGOs and humanitarian organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel to or stay in Afghanistan against FCDO advice, be aware that terrorists have a strong desire to target public places frequented by foreign nationals. This could include restaurants and hotels used by foreigners, such as the Serena in Kabul."]},{"k":"p","s":["An attack on Kabul International Airport in August 2021 killed at least 183 people. Further attacks against aviation and airports are very likely."]},{"k":"p","s":["ISKP have claimed responsibility for attacks in many types of location, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hospitals"]},{"k":"li","s":["schools"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["government, military and security establishments"]},{"k":"p","s":["Diplomatic premises may be attacked to undermine Taliban claims of security."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is likely that terrorists will conduct attacks at busy times of day, potentially coinciding with local or religious events or celebrations. In the past this has included attacks against:"]},{"k":"li","s":["schools"]},{"k":"li","s":["marketplaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["sites, communities and districts where the majority population is Shia Muslim"]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks in Afghanistan include roadside and suicide bombs either on foot or by vehicle, indirect rocket and mortar fire, direct fire, including shootings and rocket propelled grenades."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Afghanistan, make sure your accommodation is secure and review your security measures regularly. Keep others, including family and friends, informed of your travel plans. Any regular patterns of travel and behaviour could make you the target of an attack."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a very high threat of being kidnapped in Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tour operators in Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are tour operators that offer travel and guided tours to Afghanistan. FCDO continues to advise against all travel to Afghanistan, even if you are part of an organised tour group. In May 2024, three Spanish tourists were killed in a shooting while on a guided tour in Bamiyan, Central Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["The risks of detention, kidnap and other security threats to British nationals remain high."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Afghanistan is under Taliban control."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban has a very low tolerance for demonstrations and for activities perceived as dissent. Foreign nationals’ activities are viewed with suspicion. Do not do anything which could be interpreted as seeking to achieve political change through violence, or any activity inciting violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may come under suspicion if you go near sensitive sites or contact people who are of interest to the authorities for any reason."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British government will have very limited ability to help you if you get into difficulty in Afghanistan. If you are a British national already resident in Afghanistan, you should carefully consider the risk to your safety."]},{"k":"p","s":["The political situation remains uncertain and could change rapidly. Ongoing tensions between Afghanistan and Pakistan may worsen the security situation. Keep up to date with developments about the security situation and monitor local media."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not rely on previous experience of travelling in Afghanistan or previous understanding of rules, laws and society. British nationals with previous experience of operating in Afghanistan have been detained in the country since August 2021."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid demonstrations as they may turn violent and you may be arrested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Detention and possible charges"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant risk the Taliban could detain British nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban are suspicious of foreign nationals working or travelling in Afghanistan, including humanitarian workers and journalists, and it’s likely your work and movements will be closely monitored."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are detained in Afghanistan, you could face months or years in prison without clarity about the charges."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban are likely to suspect you of spying and may detain you if you are found in possession of:"]},{"k":"li","s":["weapons or explosives"]},{"k":"li","s":["tracking devices"]},{"k":"li","s":["large amounts of money"]},{"k":"li","s":["items considered unusual"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of detention is especially high if you have worked in the military or have connections to previously detained British nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are found guilty of spying or working to undermine Afghanistan’s national security, the punishment may be execution."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban do not tolerate the practice of religions other than Islam and may view religious activities that do not fit with their own version of Sunni Islam as suspicious, particularly any efforts to convert Afghan nationals to an alternative religion. Such actions are forbidden and can lead to severe penalties. The Taliban’s justice system includes lengthy imprisonment, lashings (including in public) and the death penalty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["UK government support for detainees"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British government may not be notified if you are detained. There are considerable challenges in setting up contact or access. FCDO’s ability to get any information from the authorities could be severely limited, and you may not be able to contact your next of kin."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violent street crime and home invasion including armed robbery in Afghan cities. Make sure your accommodation is secure and review your security measures regularly."]},{"k":"h","s":["Criminal kidnaps"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant risk of kidnapping of foreign nationals for ransom."]},{"k":"p","s":["Potential targets for kidnap include British tourists, British nationals working for international organisations, and British nationals of Afghan origin visiting friends and relatives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminal groups will target anyone perceived to have money for extortion purposes. Victims can be targeted or selected at random. Criminal groups may kidnap victims by stopping cars on busy roads or targeting people who are withdrawing money from banks and ATMs. Kidnap victims are held while criminals empty their bank accounts using their cash cards. Incidents include a British dual national being kidnapped at gunpoint and a British national kidnapped while withdrawing money from a bank."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no formal internationally recognised structures or processes of law in Afghanistan and foreign nationals, including British nationals, have been detained without due process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Afghanistan is an Islamic country. The country’s laws and customs are very different to those in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban do not tolerate the practice of religions other than Islam and may view religious activities that do not fit with their own version of Sunni Islam as suspicious, particularly any efforts to convert Afghan nationals to an alternative religion."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Laws on dress"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban have set codes of dress for men and women and strictly enforce them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women, including foreign nationals, must fully cover themselves in public. A woman must wear:"]},{"k":"li","s":["loose-fitting clothing to conceal her body, arms and legs"]},{"k":"li","s":["a headscarf to cover her hair"]},{"k":"li","s":["a veil to cover her face"]},{"k":"p","s":["Men must dress modestly and avoid wearing clothing such as sleeveless shirts or shorts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lack of women’s rights"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban have made it illegal for women to travel for more than 72km (44 miles) without being accompanied by their husband, father or brother (a ‘mahram’). Taliban officials regularly check transport and monitor public locations, including hospitals and schools. They can stop women from travelling, including leaving Afghanistan, and may penalise women in other ways, including detention, if they do not comply."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country."]},{"k":"p","s":["During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in a vehicle"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal food, drugs and alcohol"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are not allowed to use or bring into the country narcotics, alcohol or pork products. If you do, you could be arrested."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phones, internet access and communications"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Taliban have blocked, significantly slowed, or shut down landline, internet, and mobile services without warning in the past. This can be nationwide or localised. This can affect communication and location services on smartphones and other devices. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not rely on mobile data, non-Afghan mobile apps or international calls for personal safety"]},{"k":"li","s":["always keep an alternative means of communication and navigation with you"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure friends and family know where you are"]},{"k":"p","s":["Previous internet blackouts have also impacted flights and access to cash."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It may not be immediately clear whether taking photos could cause offence or suspicion. Avoid photographing local people without their agreement and pay close attention to local information and ways of doing things. Photographing certain buildings in Afghanistan is not allowed and may lead to detention, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["military installations"]},{"k":"li","s":["palaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["Taliban checkpoints"]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal under the Taliban and has historically always been forbidden in Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying antiquities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not buy or try to export antiquities without getting a receipt from an authorised dealer. When you leave Afghanistan the authorities may ask for proof you bought the item. If you do not have a receipt, they could detain you, and you may get a fine or prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to Afghanistan against FCDO advice, you may face problems with the authorities if you try to import foreign currency. It is illegal to carry more than 5000 US dollars through airports and more than 500 US dollars through land borders in cash, but you may not be able to use foreign-issued bank cards at ATMs and local banks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some ATMs and many banks accept foreign-issued bank cards, with restrictions on the amount of cash you can withdraw. Check with local branches."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some international money transfer services continue to operate in Afghanistan. However, payouts will be in local currency, even when the payee has requested foreign exchange."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road travel is highly dangerous. FCDO advises against all travel around Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation at Afghanistan’s border crossings remains volatile. A number of borders remain closed and if opened, can close at short notice. There have been clashes between Afghan and neighbouring forces at some border crossings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kabul International Airport does not meet international aviation safety standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," lists all known airlines in Afghanistan that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to and from the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Afghanistan is in an active earthquake zone. Consider signing up to the US Geological Survey global monitoring agency. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Floods and avalanches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rain and winter snowfall can cause significant floods, particularly outside the capital. Heavy snowfall often causes avalanches in the mountains during the winter and spring. Afghanistan lacks emergency response infrastructure, so be prepared for any situation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only very limited medical facilities are available in Afghanistan. There is no guarantee local health practitioners will be available."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have valid and ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are limited public ambulance services in Afghanistan. The telephone number for the ambulance service in Kabul is 102 and each province has a separate emergency number. If you need urgent attention, speak directly with a local medical practitioner and use local transport to get to hospital when safe to do so. Ambulances sent by hospitals may require payment or evidence of insurance before they treat you."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Afghanistan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/1/afghanistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Afghanistan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/1/afghanistan"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["diarrhoeal diseases and other gastrointestinal infections"]},{"k":"li","s":["measles and other viral infections"]},{"k":"li","s":["respiratory tuberculosis"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Afghanistan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. There are serious shortages of some medicines in Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 119 (police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no British Embassy in Afghanistan and our ability to provide help to British nationals is severely limited and cannot be delivered in person."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK government cannot help British nationals who are in Afghanistan and who wish to leave. Anyone who wants to leave Afghanistan should do so by commercial means or through a land border. FCDO cannot advise on the safety of routes to leave Afghanistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"p","s":["For information about applying for a British passport, or to check on your passport application, see ",["overseas British passport applications","https://www.gov.uk/overseas-passports"]," or ",["call the Passport Adviceline","https://www.passport.service.gov.uk/help"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/afghanistan/british-embassy-afghanistan"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":20595,"change":"Addition of information about UK Government support (see ‘Do not travel to Afghanistan’ on the ‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/misinformation-won-how-divisive-politics-doomed-canadas-carbon-tax-295644":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"810427b9254d6013e83cc4caf17a685c62bbd721b6e713c946ebb9f68628abe6","read":"https://theconversation.com/misinformation-won-how-divisive-politics-doomed-canadas-carbon-tax-295644","bytes":188734,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Misinformation won: How divisive politics doomed Canada’s carbon tax","by":[{"n":"Kathryn Harrison","r":"Professor of Political Science, University of British Columbia"},{"n":"Alice Lépissier","r":"Researcher, University of California, Santa Barbara"},{"n":"Chloé Boutron","r":"PhD Candidate in Political Science, University of British Columbia"},{"n":"Erick Lachapelle","r":"Associate professor, Département de science politique, Université de Montréal"},{"n":"Matto Mildenberger","r":"Assistant Professor of Political Science, University of California, Santa Barbara"}],"pub":"2026-11-08T15:04:58Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s consumer ",["carbon tax is dead and buried, repealed in 2025","https://www.canada.ca/en/department-finance/news/2025/03/removing-the-consumer-carbon-price-effective-april-1-2025.html"],". Given the divisive politics that surrounded the carbon tax, many are probably happy never to think about it again. However, ",["research we published last month","https://doi.org/10.1007/s10584-026-04280-8"]," offers important lessons about how toxic politics threatens the quality of Canada’s public policies and democracy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before it was repealed, we asked Canadians what the carbon tax was costing them at the pump. We found that Conservative voters were living in a different world. Compared to neighbours with similar fuel consumption — who would have been taxed roughly the same — they estimated it was costing them hundreds of dollars more every month."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our research, combined with numerous academic studies of the British Columbia carbon tax, drives home a sobering conclusion: a policy that was fair, effective at fighting climate change and even put money into most taxpayers’ pockets died because Canadians simply didn’t believe any of that."]},{"k":"h","s":["What the research found"]},{"k":"p","s":["We undertook a series of public opinion surveys to better understand Canadians’ perceptions of their carbon-tax costs and rebates, and how those impacted opposition to the carbon tax."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study, recently published in the ",["Climatic Change journal","https://link.springer.com/journal/10584"],", asked them how much they thought the carbon tax was costing them. In 2022, we asked 1,000 Canadians across five provinces detailed questions about their families’ fuel consumption, including their gasoline expenditures and utility bills. We also asked them how much they believed the carbon tax was contributing to transportation and heating fuel prices, and how much they thought their family was paying in carbon taxes monthly."]},{"k":"p","s":["We investigated perceptions of carbon-tax rebates in an ",["earlier study","https://doi.org/10.1038/s41558-021-01268-3"],". Survey respondents shared their postal codes and the number of adults and children in their household (subject to our promise not to reveal their personal information). With that information, we could calculate each respondent’s annual household rebate."]},{"k":"p","s":["In reality, those who were consuming more fossil fuels for transportation and home heating were paying proportionately more in carbon taxes. Yet we found that Canadians’ beliefs about their carbon-tax payments did not reflect their actual fossil fuel consumption."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was especially true for how much Canadians thought the carbon tax cost them at the pump, which was the main flashpoint for opposition to the policy."]},{"k":"p","s":["A member of our research team, Chloé Boutron, ",["previously reported","https://dx.doi.org/10.14288/1.0394722"]," that Canadians have remarkably accurate knowledge of gasoline prices in their community. In other words, it wasn’t that Canadians didn’t understand how much they were paying for gas, but rather how much of that cost was due to the carbon tax. By contrast, people’s perceptions of their heating costs was roughly correct."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politics shaped perceptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study found that Canadians’ beliefs about carbon-tax costs and benefits largely came down to their politics. The perceived impact of the carbon tax on gasoline and diesel costs was strongly predicted by a single factor: which political party the respondent voted for in the previous federal election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Compared to Liberal voters with similar fossil-fuel consumption and therefore similar actual carbon-tax costs, Conservative voters perceived they were paying almost $5,000 a year more in carbon taxes than their Liberal counterparts did."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political party also predicted what people thought about their rebates. Conservative voters reported receiving lower carbon-tax rebates than voters from other parties within the same province."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also found that perceived, rather than actual, costs best explained voters’ opposition to the carbon tax. When respondents received a mockup of their household’s carbon-tax rebate form, both Liberal and Conservative voters estimated their rebates more accurately."]},{"k":"p","s":["But after realizing that their rebates were higher than they thought, Conservative voters were more likely to report that meant they were paying more in carbon taxes than they were getting back. Accurate information backfired amid a hyper-partisan policy debate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["The carbon tax needs fixing, not axing — Canada needs a progressive carbon tax","https://theconversation.com/the-carbon-tax-needs-fixing-not-axing-canada-needs-a-progressive-carbon-tax-244017"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risks of misinformation"]},{"k":"p","s":["In some respects, misapprehensions about the carbon tax isn’t surprising. It was a new policy, with opaque costs. But those misunderstandings were amplified."]},{"k":"p","s":["Conservative politicians offered selective statements that could easily mislead voters — for instance, ignoring the existence of rebates or focusing on the carbon tax at a time of rising consumer costs, even though its ",["contribution to inflation","https://irpp.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Does-Emissions-Pricing-Hurt-Affordability.pdf"]," was minuscule."]},{"k":"p","s":["Already misleading messages then were further simplified via memes widely shared by right-of-centre allies on social media. The impact of misinformation was facilitated by a growing partisan divide and decline of shared news sources."]},{"k":"p","s":["And it worked. ",["Conservative party support rose in tandem with carbon-tax opposition","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2025/2/5/how-canadas-carbon-pricing-scheme-became-a-political-football"]," after 2022, ",["ultimately prompting the Liberal Party to abandon its own policy","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/carney-to-scrap-carbon-tax-1.7446908"]," leading into the 2025 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["With that track record, there’s every reason to expect future applications of the carbon tax playbook will not be limited to climate policy — nor to a single political party."]}],"chars":5199},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/hungary":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"d2046495fc7ecb97bea7d2eca9dbe525ef2f3d4feb2bca2eee9cd20df182356f","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/hungary","bytes":73111,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Hungary travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-28T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-23T16:27:57+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/hungary/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Hungary set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Hungarian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.gov.hu/eng"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hungary follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/apply-renew-passport"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel ",["without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Hungary, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-hungary-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Hungarian border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of accommodation, for example, a hotel booking"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Hungarian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.gov.hu/eng"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For residence permits, see the National Directorate-General for Aliens Policing."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Hungary with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Hungary.","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-hungary#passports-and-travel"]]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into and out of Hungary","https://nav.gov.hu/en/intormation_on_customs_matters/General_Customs_Information/Information_for_travellers_2022"],", including pets, hunting weapons, alcohol and tobacco products and some medicines. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food and drink into Hungary"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Hungary"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Hungary"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Hungary cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political demonstrations can be held in Budapest and across Hungary. Rallies often take place on important national holidays, such as 15 March (anniversary of 1848 Revolution) and 23 October (anniversary of 1956 anti-Soviet Uprising). Peaceful demonstrations have sometimes turned violent. Move away from large crowds and monitor local media to help you avoid organised demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists can be targets for petty crime. Bag-snatching and pickpocketing are common, especially in Budapest and other cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime is more likely:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on busy public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["in train stations"]},{"k":"li","s":["at markets"]},{"k":"li","s":["in places with high numbers of tourists"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by train keep a close watch on your baggage, especially as the train pulls into a station."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leave your car or motorbike in a secure location if possible to reduce the risk of it being stolen. Theft from parked vehicles is common, so always put bags out of sight and do not store valuable items in your car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams when paying bills"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some bars, clubs and restaurants might charge high amounts for food and drink. Tourists have been taken to cashpoints with demands for the money to pay the bill. Always ask to see the menu and price list before ordering food and check your bill carefully before paying. Be wary of establishments where menus do not properly display prices. Report any incidents to the police."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some taxi drivers are part of these frauds. They may receive a commission to recommend certain bars, clubs and restaurants to passengers. If a taxi driver offers to take you to a bar or club, or you are approached on the street with an invitation, be cautious. Use taxis from a reputable local company."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use official ATMs or banks. Do not change money on the street."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Use ATMs inside banks if possible, and check ATMs on the street for signs of tampering. Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read more about ",["how to avoid bank card fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of drinks being spiked, particularly in Budapest’s bars. If your drink is spiked it can make you vulnerable – for example to assault or robbery. Buy your own drinks and keep sight of them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport. You must show ID if the police ask for it, and a copy is not acceptable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Hungary have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Hungary. Budapest is generally tolerant and open. Outside of Budapest, showing affection in public may receive unwanted attention. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Festivals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are going to a summer music festival in Hungary, see FCDO’s ",["travel checklist for festivals in Europe","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/festival-travel-checklist"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the Metro, you must validate your ticket at the entrance to the station. On buses, trams or trolley buses, you must validate your ticket immediately after boarding. Remember to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your ticket until the end of your journey, as ticket inspectors can ask to see it at any time"]},{"k":"li","s":["validate a new ticket each time you change lines or mode of transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["get a special ticket for the night service network"]},{"k":"p","s":["You could get a fine if you do not follow the rules of the transport ticket system. See more information on ticket conditions from the Budapest Transport Authority."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Hungary, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Hungary guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/hungary/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Hungary. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Hungary, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check the ",["information about driving if you’re resident in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-hungary#driving-in-hungary"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving regulations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hungary has a no-alcohol driving policy. It is illegal to drink any alcohol and then drive in Hungary."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must use dipped headlights on roads outside towns even in daytime."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Roads that require an e-vignette (toll)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to use major highways in Hungary, you must ",["buy a motorway e-vignette","https://ematrica.nemzetiutdij.hu/en/vignette-purchase/vehicle-data-vignette-selection"]," in advance of your journey. The vignette is a form of electronic toll. If you use the roads without buying an e-vignette, you will get a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transporting humanitarian or medical aid"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to transit through Hungary with consignments of humanitarian aid or medical aid, contact the ",["Hungarian Embassy in the UK","https://london.mfa.gov.hu/eng"]," in advance to apply for a waiver of normal haulage fees."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when travelling by train and keep your belongings in sight. Take extra care on night trains. Never leave bags unattended. Travel with companions where possible and lock your compartment from the inside."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can access ",["local forecasts and weather warnings","https://www.met.hu/en/idojaras/index.php"]," for Hungary. Follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Hungary","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/103/hungary#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Hungary","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/103/hungary"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Hungary"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hungary-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Hungary, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-hungary"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Hungary"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find?serviceType=lawyers&country=Hungary"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Hungary"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Hungary"]," in Hungary"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hungary-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/hungary-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/hungary/british-embassy-budapest"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/hungary/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Hungary","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-hungary"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16496,"change":"Removal of information about restrictions to LGBT+ marches and events ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/ketika-anak-lakukan-tindak-kriminal-cukupkah-aturan-kita-melindungi-keluarga-korban-295969":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"37aacd1f23ab79979bd2c459809091a402ae59120ded0173a049eea939a3c1c7","read":"https://theconversation.com/ketika-anak-lakukan-tindak-kriminal-cukupkah-aturan-kita-melindungi-keluarga-korban-295969","bytes":181454,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ketika anak lakukan tindak kriminal, cukupkah aturan kita melindungi keluarga korban?","by":[{"n":"Arya Wijaya Pramodha Wardhana","r":"Dosen Departemen Informasi dan Perpustakaan, Universitas Airlangga"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T08:01:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Pembinaan anak pelaku kekerasan harus terukur dan mencegah pengulangan."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Hak korban atas pemulihan dan keadilan tidak boleh terabaikan."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Negara perlu memperkuat pengawasan, pendampingan keluarga, dan pencegahan kekerasan berulang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seorang anak dengan disabilitas di Rungkut, Surabaya, meninggal diduga karena perundungan dan ",["kekerasan oleh anak-anak lain","https://surabaya.kompas.com/read/2026/10/19/094912478/nasib-terduga-pelaku-perundungan-anak-disabilitas-di-surabaya-ditentukan"],". Kepolisian, Senin 19 Oktober lalu, mengumumkan ",["pembinaan enam bulan di Rumah Perubahan","https://kabarjawatimur.com/2026/10/kasus-anak-10-tahun-meninggal-di-rungkut-pelaku-anak-dibina-di-rumah-perubahan-selama-6-bulan/"]," bagi anak berusia 10 tahun yang diduga terlibat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengadilan Negeri Surabaya kemudian ",["dilaporkan menetapkan penempatan sementara anak lain yang berstatus saksi di pondok pesantren","https://jatim.suara.com/read/2026/10/26/115920/jerit-hati-orang-tua-saat-anak-berkebutuhan-khusus-menjadi-korban-perundungan-hingga-tewas"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["“Namanya juga anak-anak”: Ungkapan toksik yang mewajarkan perundungan anak difabel","https://theconversation.com/namanya-juga-anak-anak-ungkapan-toksik-yang-mewajarkan-perundungan-anak-difabel-295888"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Penanganan kasus ini memunculkan pertanyaan penting tentang bagaimana hukum di Indonesia mengadili anak yang diduga melakukan kekerasan sekaligus menjamin hak korban. Selama ini, ",["hukum pidana anak","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/39061/uu-no-11-tahun-2012"]," amat rapat melindungi anak, tetapi bolong ketika dipakai menjaga korban."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kita tidak perlu menuntut anak diperlakukan seperti orang dewasa. Namun, perlindungan terhadap anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum tetap harus menjamin keadilan bagi keluarga korban."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ini menjadi ujian bagi kemampuan negara untuk memastikan pembinaan berjalan efektif, korban dipulihkan, dan kekerasan tidak berulang."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pembinaan bukan sekadar memenuhi waktu"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Pasal 21 UU Sistem Peradilan Pidana Anak (SPPA)","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/39061/uu-no-11-tahun-2012"]," mengatur anak di bawah 12 tahun terduga tindak pidana dapat dikembalikan kepada orang tua atau diikutsertakan dalam program pendidikan, pembinaan, dan pembimbingan paling lama enam bulan. Masa ini dapat diperpanjang hingga enam bulan berdasarkan evaluasi Balai Pemasyarakatan (Bapas)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adapun ",["Pasal 40 dan 41 KUHP baru","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/234935/uu-no-1-tahun-2023"]," turut menegaskan bahwa anak di bawah 12 tahun tidak dapat dimintai pertanggungjawaban pidana. ",["General Comment No. 24","https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3899429/files/CRC_C_GC_24-EN.pdf"]," Komite Hak Anak PBB bahkan mendorong negara menetapkan batas usia pertanggungjawaban pidana minimal 14 tahun."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, kebal pidana bukan berarti negara cukup mengembalikannya ke keluarga atau menempatkannya di lembaga pembinaan. Pembinaan harus menjawab mengapa anak melakukan kekerasan, bagaimana perilakunya dapat berubah, dan bagaimana risiko pengulangan dapat dicegah."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya, pembinaan selama ini bukan jaminan bisa menghentikan aksi mengintimidasi teman, memukul, atau merendahkan orang lain. Karena itu, pembenahan harus mengukur perubahan perilaku, pemahaman dampak kekerasan, dan kemampuan mengendalikan tindakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Negara membutuhkan rencana tindak lanjut, bukan sekadar laporan bahwa program telah selesai karena risiko kekerasan masih tinggi hingga saat ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Yang harus dilakukan jika anak Anda justru adalah pelaku bullying, bukan korban","https://theconversation.com/yang-harus-dilakukan-jika-anak-anda-justru-adalah-pelaku-bullying-bukan-korban-187783"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Beban bukan tanggungan korban"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam mayoritas kasus kekerasan anak, keluarga korban ",["kerap luput dari perhatian","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0190740911001794"],". Padahal merekalah yang kehilangan anak, tetapi juga membutuhkan kepastian tentang pemulihan, pendampingan psikologis, dan perkembangan penanganan perkara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam kasus anak di bawah 12 tahun, muncul persoalan yang perlu dijawab: bagaimana keluarga korban mengakses restitusi ketika tidak ada proses pemidanaan terhadap anak yang diduga terlibat? Mekanisme yang mensyaratkan proses dan putusan perkara berisiko sulit diakses dalam situasi seperti ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anak dengan disabilitas berhak memperoleh perlindungan khusus berdasarkan ",["UU Perlindungan Anak","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/38723/uu-no-35-tahun-2014"]," dan ",["UU Nomor 8 Tahun 2016 tentang Penyandang Disabilitas","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/37251/uu-no-8-tahun-2016"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Pasal 90 UU SPPA","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/39061/uu-no-11-tahun-2012"]," telah menjamin hak anak korban atas rehabilitasi medis dan sosial, jaminan keselamatan, serta informasi perkembangan perkara. Hak tersebut harus diwujudkan dalam layanan nyata, bukan berhenti sebagai ketentuan tertulis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan lainnya adalah pemenuhan ganti kerugian. ",["Peraturan Pemerintah Nomor 43 Tahun 2017","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/51733/pp-no-43-tahun-2017"]," mengatur restitusi bagi anak korban, sementara ",["UU Nomor 3 Tahun 2026 tentang Pelindungan Saksi dan Korban","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/349942/uu-no-3-tahun-2026"]," memperluas pengaturan restitusi dan kompensasi, meskipun kompensasi tidak berlaku otomatis bagi semua jenis tindak pidana."]},{"k":"p","s":["Gugatan perdata berdasarkan ",["Pasal 1367 KUHPerdata","https://www.hukumonline.com/stories/article/lt669f5de14e06c/tanggung-jawab-renteng-atas-kerugian-menurut-pasal-1367-kuh-perdata/"]," dapat dipertimbangkan sesuai unsur dan fakta hukumnnya. Namun, keluarga yang sedang berduka tidak semestinya harus mencari sendiri keadilannya. Aparat dan Lembaga Perlindungan Saksi dan Korban (LPSK) perlu aktif menjelaskan hak serta pilihan pemulihan yang tersedia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pendampingan orang tua pelaku"]},{"k":"p","s":["Setiap kali anak melakukan kekerasan, orang tua kerap menjadi sasaran tudingan. Namun bukan berarti setiap tindakan pidana merupakan kelalaian orang tua."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Undang-undang","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/38723/uu-no-35-tahun-2014"]," memang mewajibkan orang tua mengasuh, mendidik, melindungi anak, bahkan melarang ",["penelantaran anak","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/38723/uu-no-35-tahun-2014"],". Namun, pertanggungjawaban pidana harus didasarkan pada perbuatan dan kesalahan orang tua sendiri yang dapat dibuktikan, bukan semata-mata karena anaknya melakukan kekerasan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Orang tua yang kesulitan mengelola perilaku anak membutuhkan pendampingan pekerja sosial, konseling keluarga, dan akses pendidikan pengasuhan. Jika ditemukan dugaan penelantaran, tentunya harus ditindak tegas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan demikian, tanggung jawab keluarga tidak berhenti pada mencari siapa yang salah. Negara juga harus memastikan keluarga memiliki dukungan untuk mencegah kekerasan berulang."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["True Crime Community: Saat internet menjadi tempat anak belajar kekerasan","https://theconversation.com/true-crime-community-saat-internet-menjadi-tempat-anak-belajar-kekerasan-292986"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Pengawasan dan pencegahan harus sejalan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Persoalan berikutnya adalah pengawasan. ",["Peraturan Pemerintah Nomor 65 Tahun 2015","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/5641/pp-no-65-tahun-2015"]," mengatur evaluasi Balai Permasyarakatan dan kewajiban lembaga pembinaan melaporkan perkembangan anak setiap bulan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, Keputusan yang menyangkut kehidupan anak tidak boleh bergantung pada kebijakan informal tanpa evaluasi. Penempatan sementara anak saksi di pondok pesantren juga membutuhkan kejelasan mengenai dasar keputusan, durasi, pengawasan, serta jaminan pendidikan dan keselamatannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perlindungan identitas juga tidak kalah penting. ",["Pasal 19 UU SPPA","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/39061/uu-no-11-tahun-2012"]," mewajibkan kerahasiaan identitas anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum, termasuk anak korban dan saksi. Ini perlu diperbarui di era media sosial dan digital seperti saat ini mudah sekali mencari informasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pencegahan juga harus menjangkau sekolah dan lingkungan pergaulan. ",["Meta-analisis terhadap 107 penelitian","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27784727/"]," menemukan bahwa anak dengan penyakit kronis atau disabilitas memiliki risiko lebih tinggi menjadi korban perundungan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sementara itu, ",["tinjauan sistematis tentang program antiperundungan di sekolah","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33715780/"]," mengungkap bahwa sekolah tidak cukup hanya menghukum pelaku setelah kejadian. Mereka perlu memiliki mekanisme pelaporan yang aman, pengawasan, pendidikan inklusif, dan keterlibatan teman sebaya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada akhirnya, ukuran keberhasilan hukum pidana anak bukan pada seberapa berat hukuman yang dijatuhkan. Ukurannya adalah apakah anak yang melakukan kekerasan mendapat pembinaan efektif, korban memperoleh pemulihan, dan lingkungan mampu mencegah kejadian serupa."]},{"k":"p","s":["Melindungi anak bukan berarti membiarkan korban berjuang sendirian. Pembinaan tanpa pemulihan korban dan pencegahan hanya akan membuat negara sibuk menangani akibat, bukan mencegah kekerasan berikutnya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Konflik Nikita Mirzani dan putrinya: momen refleksi efektivitas kebijakan perlindungan anak di Indonesia","https://theconversation.com/konflik-nikita-mirzani-dan-putrinya-momen-refleksi-efektivitas-kebijakan-perlindungan-anak-di-indonesia-240363"]]}],"chars":7050},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iceland":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"b0e45c3f7a4dad3c997277a392d95c4fee43d7fe3889bbdab3ddd66ce8ad752c","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/iceland","bytes":70754,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Iceland travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-28T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:17:40+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Recently there has been a series of volcanic eruptions on the Reykjanes peninsula in south-west Iceland."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more details see ",["Extreme weather and natural disasters","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iceland/safety-and-security#extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iceland/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Iceland set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Icelandic Embassy in the UK","https://www.government.is/diplomatic-missions/embassy-of-iceland-in-london/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iceland follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel to the Schengen area, which includes Iceland, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period without a visa. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirements for ",["working in Iceland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-iceland-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries as well, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Icelandic border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["show you have enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to work or study, or for other reasons, you must meet the Icelandic entry requirements. Check what type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Icelandic Directorate of Immigration","https://island.is/en/o/directorate-of-immigration"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you‘re in Iceland with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Iceland.","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-iceland#passports-and-travel"]]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo.There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Iceland guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/104/iceland#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Iceland","https://www.skatturinn.is/english/individuals/customs-matters/travelling-to-iceland/duty-free-imports/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Whale products"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import whale products from Iceland into the UK. You could get a fine of up to £5,000 or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into or out of Iceland"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare if you’re carrying any currency worth 10,000 euros or more."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food and drink into Iceland"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into Iceland","https://www.mast.is/en/travel"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Iceland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Iceland, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low but petty theft and antisocial behaviour can occur, particularly around bars in downtown Reykjavík. Take sensible precautions and keep your belongings safe."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not have to carry your passport with you, but it is sensible to have some form of ID, such as a photocard driving licence. You could also carry a copy of your passport’s photo page as ID. Keep your passport somewhere safe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke or use e-cigarettes in restaurants, bars, public transport and public buildings, and you could get a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, even small amounts, including cannabis and khat carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Iceland have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is legal in Iceland and same-sex relationships are recognised in law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hiking, mountaineering and other adventure sports have specific risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read the Safe Travel Iceland guides"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave travel plans and contact details with your hotel, or on Safe Travel Iceland"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a phone with you"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["When hiking, choose a trail suited for your level of experience. Conditions in Iceland could be different to what you’re used to."]},{"k":"p","s":["Going too close to the ocean, cliff edges and hot springs are common causes of accidents in Iceland."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take enough food, equipment, clothing and emergency rations for the worst-case scenario. Use a map, compass, GPS and phone."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Iceland, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Iceland guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/iceland/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of or risk a sizeable fine up to £500. Follow speed limits, keep dipped headlights on year-round, and have suitable tyres, including tyres for winter weather when needed. Drink driving limits are also lower than the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Iceland for up to 30 days. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you bring your own car, check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive it outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving in Iceland can be very different to the UK, the weather can change quickly and make driving conditions challenging at times. Speed limits are lower than in the UK and the distances between towns are far greater."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some main routes can be gravel or dirt tracks. Roads can be narrower than you might be familiar with. Some routes, including bridges, are only a single lane with passing areas. On gravel and loose surfaces, reduce your speed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many highland tracks are only open for a short part of the summer. Some roads, such as in the highlands or interior roads, require 4-wheel drive. Drive slowly (5 to 10 kilometres per hour) when you cross rivers. River levels can change quickly, even within the same day."]},{"k":"p","s":["The weather can cause damage to rental cars that is not covered by insurance. Strong winds are common and can throw sand or ash up, damaging paintwork. British tourists have had to pay large amounts of money to repair damage to hire cars caused by sand and ash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Breakdown recovery costs, especially in remote areas, can be high."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["road and weather advice from the Icelandic Road Administration","https://www.road.is/"],". They also have information on off-road driving, which is strictly controlled."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electric Scooters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Riding a scooter after consuming alcohol is prohibited by law in Iceland. The same law as driving a car under the influence applies and will resort in a fine and or charges."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions and earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Volcanic eruptions and earthquakes are common in Iceland given the country’s geography. In the event of an eruption or wider seismic activity, always follow the latest advice issued by the authorities, including on areas to avoid and actions to take if air quality is affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since December 2023, there have been a series of volcanic eruptions on the Reykjanes peninsula in south-west Iceland, the latest started on 16 July 2025. These eruptions have affected the town of Grindavik and the surrounding area. The capital city, Reykjavik, Keflavik International Airport and the rest of Iceland have not been affected by this series of eruptions."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is likely that there will be further eruptions on the Reykjanes peninsula. You should closely monitor local media for updates and always follow the authorities’ advice on travel to, or near to, the area of an ongoing eruption. Gas pollution levels can quickly exceed dangerous levels in the immediate vicinity of an eruption site. Depending on weather conditions, while an eruption is ongoing gas pollution and volcanic haze may also spread beyond the immediate area so pay particular attention to local alerts and advice. Never attempt to walk on newly solidified lava as the surface crust can break without warning."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regularly check for alerts and advice from:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Icelandic Met Office","https://en.vedur.is/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Safe Travel Iceland","https://safetravel.is/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Icelandic Environment and Energy agency on gas pollution","https://loftgaedi.is/en?zoomLevel=7&lat=64.894972&lng=-18.675028"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["the Icelandic tourist board","https://www.visiticeland.com/article/volcano-info"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Almannavarnir Facebook page","https://www.facebook.com/Almannavarnir/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The Government of Iceland monitors all seismic and volcanic activity closely and infrastructure is robustly designed, but not all events can be anticipated and can pose risks to your travel plans. This could include travel delays and cancellations due to rock falls and landslides, sudden flooding, or poisonous volcanic gases near eruption sites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Further information on volcanic eruptions and earthquakes in Iceland can be found from the following organisations:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Icelandic Department of Civil Protection and Emergency Management","https://www.almannavarnir.is/english/"]," – includes health and safety advice"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Icelandic Road and Coastal Administration","https://www.road.is/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Institute of Earth Sciences","https://earthice.hi.is/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["London Volcanic Ash Advisory Centre","https://www.metoffice.gov.uk/services/transport/aviation/regulated/vaac/advisories/archive"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Icelandic National Broadcasting Service","https://www.ruv.is/english"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Arctic travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Iceland is in the Arctic Circle: emergency medical assistance and search and rescue may be limited in some areas. See ",["Arctic travel safety advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arctic-travel-safety-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Iceland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/104/iceland#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Iceland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/104/iceland"],", including biting insects and ticks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Iceland"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Iceland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/iceland-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Iceland, you can ",["now use the Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)","https://www.nhsbsa.nhs.uk/get-healthcare-cover-travelling-abroad/where-you-can-use-your-card"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Iceland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-iceland#healthcare"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Iceland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Safe Travel Iceland"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling around Iceland, leave details of your travel plans with Safe Travel Iceland in case you need help from the Icelandic emergency services."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Iceland"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Iceland"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Iceland"]," in Iceland"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Iceland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/iceland-bereavement-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Iceland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/iceland-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/iceland/british-embassy-reykjavik"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/iceland/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":17766,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nepal":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"4dcd35ff1afd572e3ccc1fae43ea0f432c978291761bdc1936b1bc15bf18c58d","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/nepal","bytes":77796,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Nepal travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-06T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-01T13:09:36+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Flash flood in the Rasuwa district and the Nepal-China border area"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 26 August 2026, major flooding in Rasuwa district and the Nepal-China border area caused widespread damage. Buildings, roads, other transport and communications infrastructure have been severely damaged. Other areas in Nepal, including Gorkha, Nuwakot and Dhading, have also been affected."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nepalese authorities and emergency services are responding. The authorities have warned of the risk of further flooding. Areas affected by flooding and landslides may remain unstable. Further heavy rainfall or an earthquake could trigger additional landslides, rockfalls and other hazards, particularly in mountainous areas. The situation may change rapidly."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling in the region, follow the advice of the Nepalese government and local authorities, be alert to the changing situation and monitor local media for updates. The Nepalese government has established a toll-free emergency Nepalese language number, 1234, and a dedicated hotline 1144 accessible in Nepal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Consular assistance remains available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week for anyone affected who requires support from the UK Government."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are affected and need assistance from the UK Government call:"]},{"k":"li","s":["from Nepal +977 (0)14237100"]},{"k":"li","s":["from India +91 11 2419 2100"]},{"k":"li","s":["from the UK +44 (0) 207 008 5000"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nepal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated. See the ‘Getting Help’ page for further information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nepal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK Government’s understanding of Nepal’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Nepal set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Nepal Embassy in the UK","https://uk.nepalembassy.gov.np/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To avoid problems at immigration, make sure your passport has an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after your date of entry into Nepal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["At border control, you may need to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a travel insurance document which has cover for healthcare costs including repatriation and other emergencies while you are in Nepal"]},{"k":"li","s":["confirmation of where you will spend your first night, for example, a hotel booking"]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to visit Nepal for up to 90 days."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply online for a visa on arrival","https://nepaliport.immigration.gov.np/"]," up to 15 days in advance of your arrival. Using your submission receipt, you then collect and pay for your visa at the airport. You can also apply using the forms or terminals available at the airport, then ",["queue up to get the visa","https://ntb.gov.np/plan-your-trip/before-you-come/tourist-visa"],". You can pay by card, but you should have cash as a back-up, with US dollars being the preferred currency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Alternatively you can ",["apply for a tourist visa in advance","https://nepaliport.immigration.gov.np/onlinevisa-mission/application"]," and collect it from the Nepal Embassy in the UK or in another country. Applying in advance can reduce the time it takes to pass through immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Visas are available for several lengths of stay at various costs. Look on the ",["immigration department website for the options","https://www.immigration.gov.np/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["extend your visa online","https://nepaliport.immigration.gov.np/"]," to up to a total of 150 days in one year."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overstaying your visa in Nepal is a serious crime and can lead to significant fines or imprisonment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Nepal, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine, if you’re coming from certain countries with a transmission risk"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Nepal guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/159/nepal#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Nepal. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bringing precious metals into Nepal is strictly regulated. You can carry gold ornaments up to 50 grams and silver ornaments up to 100 grams. If you bring in undeclared gold or silver, you may:"]},{"k":"li","s":["get a fine equivalent to the value of the goods"]},{"k":"li","s":["go to prison for between one month and 5 years depending upon the value of the goods"]},{"k":"li","s":["have the goods confiscated"]},{"k":"li","s":["be detained during the proceedings"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into and out of Nepal"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare on a customs form on arrival any amount above the value of 5,000 US dollars in banknotes or 10,000 dollars in notes and travellers cheques combined. Customs will give a certified declaration, which you must keep."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will need to convert all your Nepali currency before you leave Nepal, and the bank or exchange counter at the airport may ask you for the declaration."]},{"k":"p","s":["ATMs are not reliable outside main tourist sites."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Nepal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Nepal, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals. Be vigilant in public places and take local advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Civil disorder"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political protests, demonstrations and strikes are fairly common in Nepal."]},{"k":"p","s":["These can start at short notice and may lead to violent clashes between protesters and law enforcement. Protests cause disruption to transport and the authorities may increase the police presence or impose a curfew."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid any demonstrations"]},{"k":"li","s":["check local media for updates"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the direction of local authorities"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s a low rate of serious crime in Nepal but take precautions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Watch out for pickpockets and bag-snatchers, particularly in airports, on buses and in areas popular with foreign nationals like Thamel, Sanepa and Kupondol in Kathmandu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when walking around at night. Assaults and robberies are more likely in the evening in poorly lit areas. Avoid walking on your own and do not carry large sums of cash. Keep valuables in a hotel safe if possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women have been sexually assaulted in tourist areas such as Thamel and Sanepa in Kathmandu. Be cautious, especially when alone after dark. See ",["Advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be wary of accepting drinks from strangers and do not leave drinks unattended."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and Methanol Poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been isolated reports of some trekking guides taking inexperienced trekkers to high altitudes too quickly, and then calling in expensive helicopter medivacs from which the guides take a cut. Be wary of trekking deals that look very cheap and may be scams."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should carry your passport with you. Leave a copy in a safe place or with friends and family in the UK."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visiting holy places"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid wearing shorts and sleeveless tops in temples and other holy places. Remove shoes before entering certain holy places. Non-Hindus are not permitted inside certain parts of Hindu temples."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for drugs related offences are severe. If you are caught with even small amounts of marijuana, you can go to prison for over 5 years, usually after a long and expensive legal process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some skincare products and e-cigarette refills may contain ingredients that are illegal in Nepal such as cannabidiol (CBD). If the police find you with products containing CBD, they may seize them and charge you with drug possession."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Nepal is generally open and tolerant to LGBT+ issues, and same-sex relations are not illegal. However, showing affection in public, irrespective of sexuality or gender, is viewed by Nepalis as inappropriate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. Nepal is a signatory to the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of Wild Fauna and Flora (CITES), which bans trade of wildlife products without a permit. If you are caught buying or trafficking such goods, or knowingly assisting anyone to do so, you will get a fine or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Trekking in Nepal"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a valid permit and a Trekking Information Management System (TIMS) card to enter Nepal’s main trekking regions. See the ",["Nepal Tourism Board TIMS card requirement","https://ntb.gov.np/en/plan-your-trip/before-you-come/tims-card"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not trek alone. All foreign independent trekkers (FITs) must use a local guide or porter while trekking in Nepal’s national parks and protected areas. Always observe national park regulations and follow your guide’s instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you ignore the requirements, you may be fined or removed from protected areas. Check the ",["Nepal Tourism Board website","https://ntb.gov.np/en/latest-travel-updates"]," for further information or updates."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of hazards all year round, especially above 3,000m. There could be:"]},{"k":"li","s":["sudden weather changes and potential storms"]},{"k":"li","s":["avalanches and snow drifts"]},{"k":"li","s":["landslides, rockfalls and flooding"]},{"k":"li","s":["glacial crevasses and hollows"]},{"k":"li","s":["altitude sickness"]},{"k":"li","s":["sun exposure"]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a reputable trekking agency or guide"]},{"k":"li","s":["take note of weather forecasts and conditions"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you’re physically fit and have not overestimated your abilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["take warm clothes and wet weather gear"]},{"k":"li","s":["use sun block (SPF20 or higher) and sunglasses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure your insurance includes cover for mountain rescue services and helicopter costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get ",["live updates on trekking conditions in Nepal","https://www.facebook.com/taan.np/"],". You can also follow national weather forecasts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Internal flights in high mountain areas can be delayed by poor weather conditions and cancellations are common. Carry enough funds in case of delays, particularly in remote areas, where ATMs may not be available and credit cards not accepted."]},{"k":"p","s":["In remote areas, including long stretches of the Annapurna Circuit trek, mobile phone coverage is limited. Consider renting a satellite phone and make sure your friends and family know you will be out of contact."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volunteering and adventure travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Research any organisation or company you’re planning to use before committing yourself. See ",["Volunteering and adventure travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nepal’s Social Welfare Council has a list of registered volunteer organisations. You can ask for a copy by sending an email to: info@swc.org.np."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy has received reports of volunteer opportunities at orphanages which are profit-orientated organisations rather than charities. If you’re volunteering at this type of organisation, you could be contributing to child exploitation. Contact the Nepali Central Child Welfare Board on +977 1-5010045 and 5010046 to check before signing up to volunteer for one of these organisations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Nepal, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and read the ",["International Drivers Association Nepal driving guide","https://internationaldriversassociation.com/nepal-driving-guide"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a ",["1968 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence to drive in Nepal. The 1949 IDP is not accepted any more. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your IDP when driving, as well as your vehicle registration documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road accidents are a major cause of death and disability in Nepal. The causes include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["overloading vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["negligence of drivers"]},{"k":"li","s":["mechanical failure"]},{"k":"li","s":["speeding"]},{"k":"li","s":["poor road conditions"]},{"k":"li","s":["an increasing number of unregulated private vehicles"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road conditions are poor, especially during the monsoon season or in mountain areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["By law only the driver of a vehicle is required to wear a seatbelt, or a helmet when driving a motorbike. You can still use seatbelts for passengers, which are fitted in some taxis. Motorbike rentals will always provide helmets for passengers if requested."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bus travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bus accidents are common in Nepal and there are a number of accidents resulting in fatalities every year. Buses are often overcrowded, poorly regulated and poorly maintained. Speeding, low driving standards and poor road conditions contribute to the risk of accidents. Do not travel on overloaded or overcrowded buses, or at night. Tourist buses usually offer a higher standard of comfort and safety."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air crashes can have a variety of causes and are not necessarily linked with poor safety standards or non-compliance with international safety standards. However, there have been a number of fatal accidents and air crashes across Nepal in the commercial air transport sector, involving planes and helicopters. Over the last 5 years, this includes a number of separate incidents and at least 100 deaths."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["UK Air Safety List (ASL)","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/uk-air-safety-list"]," lists all known airlines in Nepal that do not meet international safety standards and are banned from operating commercial air services to or from the UK. Check the UK Air Safety List when considering whether to fly and which airlines to fly with. The list is maintained by the Department for Transport, based on advice from the ",["UK Civil Aviation Authority","https://www.caa.co.uk/Commercial-Industry/Airlines/Licensing/Requirements-and-guidance/Third-Country-Operator-Certificates"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Currently no Nepali airline meets the international safety standards and so all are listed on the ASL. This means they are all banned from operating commercial air services to or from the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoon"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel during the monsoon season (normally June to October) can be hazardous. Flooding and landslides can lead to impassable roads, delays to journeys, or cut off towns and villages for days at a time. If you travel by road during monsoon season you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the road is open"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to change or cancel your plans at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["take equipment, medication and enough supplies to cover any emergencies or possible delays"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nepal government Meteorological Forecasting Division provides weather updates (in English) and flood forecasts during the monsoon. You can also access the ",["Department of Hydrology and Meteorology flood monitoring service","https://www.dhm.gov.np/hydrology/floodMonitoring"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earth tremors are common across Nepal. The lack of emergency equipment and poorly resourced medical facilities is likely to worsen an earthquake’s impact. British Embassy assistance will be slow to reach you if you are in a remote area."]},{"k":"p","s":["The National Society of Earthquake Technology (NSET) gives advice on what to do in an earthquake, including ‘ ",["Ten tips on earthquake safety","https://www.nset.org.np/nset2012/index.php/menus/menuid-62/submenuid-90"],"’. Check with your tour operator to find out what contingency plans they have for an earthquake."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following a significant earthquake you should expect transport, accommodation and basic services in affected areas to be disrupted. Relief efforts are likely to be a priority for the authorities. Check with your tour company or hotel for further information on whether travel to an area is possible or appropriate."]},{"k":"h","s":["Building safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Building, fire and electrical protection standards in Nepal are not always the same as in the UK. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of electrocution risks, for example, exposed wiring"]},{"k":"li","s":["check fire precautions, including access to fire exits"]},{"k":"li","s":["check whether your accommodation has a working fire alarm"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of the risks of exposure to carbon monoxide. Carbon monoxide is a highly poisonous gas that is impossible to detect without an alarm. It can be produced by fires, charcoal grills or incorrectly installed gas equipment, and a lack of appropriate ventilation is dangerous. Find out more about ",["how to stay safe and the symptoms to look out for","https://www.energy-uk.org.uk/customers/carbon-monoxide/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no central public ambulance service. Some private providers operate in the main cities. In an emergency, call the nearest hospital. FCDO has a ",["list of some of the hospitals in Kathmandu and Pokhara","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nepal-list-of-doctors"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Nepal","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/159/nepal#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Nepal,","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/159/nepal"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["air pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Nepal, particularly in tourist and trekking areas. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Nepal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical treatment is expensive at western travellers’ clinics in Nepal. Healthcare is poor in most places outside the Kathmandu Valley and Pokhara. It may be difficult to get rapid helicopter evacuation if you fall ill or suffer a serious accident in a remote area of the country. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad, repatriation and evacuation by helicopter. This usually costs between £1,000 and £2,000 or more per flying hour."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Kathmandu and Pokhara","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nepal-list-of-doctors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Nepal"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 100"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Tourist police","https://www.tourism.gov.np/pages/tourist-police/9"]," (good English language skills): 1144"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 102"]},{"k":"h","s":["Nepal tourist police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist police in Kathmandu : 01 5347041"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourist police for incidents in Thamel (Kathmandu): 009 77 9851289453"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Nepal"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Nepal"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Nepal"]," in Nepal"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Nepal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nepal-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Nepal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/nepal-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/nepal/british-embassy-kathmandu"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nepal/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Nepal","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-nepal"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21947,"change":"Removal of information about the Family Assistance Centre at the British Embassy Kathmandu (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/a-thank-you-on-veterans-day-wont-close-the-growing-military-civilian-gap-294008":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"05bc1b520592f69640d943d2a8f4c42ed9baeec7b5deeb5b616a3132a6286b1b","read":"https://theconversation.com/a-thank-you-on-veterans-day-wont-close-the-growing-military-civilian-gap-294008","bytes":184363,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"A thank-you on Veterans Day won’t close the growing military-civilian gap","by":[{"n":"Scott Parrott","r":"Professor of Media Effects, School of Journalism and Mass Communications, University of South Carolina"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T13:41:14Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When the voice came over the plane’s PA system, it seemed familiar yet surprising: “Hello, everybody.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["“What?!” a passenger shouted, shocked. Others laughed and rose from their seats as former President Barack Obama appeared in person and ",["welcomed the airplane of veterans","https://abcnews.com/Politics/obama-surprises-veterans-flight-dc-special-veterans-day/story?id=127410327"]," to Washington before Veterans Day in 2025. They had flown from Wisconsin to Ronald Reagan Washington National Airport aboard an Honor Flight to see the capital’s monuments to military service."]},{"k":"p","s":["“I wanted to stop by and just say thank you for your extraordinary service – to you, your family,” Obama said in brief remarks ",["later posted to social media","https://x.com/BarackObama/status/1988230502197649568"],". “The sacrifices that all of you made to protect our country is something that will always be honored.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Obama’s post was one of 399,000 references to veterans on the social media platform X on Veterans Day last year, Nov. 11, 2025. The annual holiday was established to “solemnly remember the sacrifices of all those who fought so valiantly on the seas, in the air and on foreign shores, to preserve our heritage of freedom,” as ",["President Dwight D. Eisenhower proclaimed","https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/proclamation-3071-veterans-day-1954"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The hundreds of thousands of posts are compelling to me ",["as a social scientist","https://sc.edu/study/colleges_schools/cic/faculty-staff/parrott_scott.php"]," who studies how veterans are represented in the media. The volume of commentary illustrates Americans’ desire to recognize veterans, but it also captures the transience of public attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["By the following Tuesday, Nov. 18, 2025, the number of references to veterans plummeted by 374,000, or nearly 94%. The news cycle had moved on."]},{"k":"p","s":["The shift was not particularly surprising. ",["My research shows","https://doi.org/10.21061/jvs.v8i1.311"]," that social media mentions of veterans peak in positive sentiment at two points each year: Veterans Day and Memorial Day. The rest of the time, the conversations on social media are largely driven by news outlets releasing stories and politicians announcing programs and events."]},{"k":"p","s":["Indeed, social and other mass media play a role in what experts describe as ",["a military-civilian gap","https://apnews.com/article/military-who-serves-us-america-250-7e3efd3353bac98cc904b8c1561cd00b"],". Put simply, while U.S. adults hold the military in high regard, they do not understand the institution or the experiences of its personnel despite its importance in domestic and international affairs and its ",["US$900 billion in taxpayer funding","https://www.armed-services.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/passage_fy26_ndaa_executive_summary.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This military-civilian gap can create problems ",["when it comes to military recruitment","https://www.war.gov/News/Feature-Stories/Story/Article/1850344/dod-official-cites-widening-military-civilian-gap/"],", civilians’ ability to identify with neighbors who serve and ",["veterans reintegrating into civilian society","https://doi.org/10.1037/ort0000541"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["The military-civilian gap"]},{"k":"p","s":["The military-civilian gap exists in part because, since the draft ended in 1973, the share of Americans who have served in the armed forces has declined. Only about ",["6% of adults were veterans","https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/11/08/the-changing-face-of-americas-veteran-population/"]," in 2022, a decline from 18% in 1980. Compounding the issue, ",["a decreasing proportion of U.S. adults","https://www.pewresearch.org/social-trends/2011/11/23/the-military-civilian-gap-fewer-family-connections/"]," personally know someone who has served. That means much of the population is learning about military life through mass media representation."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Journalists gravitate toward stories","https://owl.purdue.edu/owl/subject_specific_writing/journalism_and_journalistic_writing/components_of_newsworthiness.html"]," in which the subject matter is timely, emotional or full of conflict, because these qualities engage audiences. They operate on tight deadlines with limited resources. They also face ",["restricted access to the Pentagon","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/judge-orders-pentagon-to-lift-policy-requiring-journalists-to-be-accompanied-by-an-escort"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["That means news outlets may be more inclined to cover a holiday, charity event or violent crime involving veterans than to take deep dives into the military budget or examine the role of veteran-owned businesses in the local economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Because of this, veterans end up typecast as heroes or victims of their service."]},{"k":"p","s":["Politicians also influence which issues people in the U.S. see in the news or discuss on social media, but the share of ",["members of Congress with military experience","https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2023/11/08/the-changing-face-of-americas-veteran-population/"]," has plummeted since the 1970s."]},{"k":"h","s":["Veterans in the media"]},{"k":"p","s":["In a 2018 study, our research team examined how news organizations in all 50 states ",["represented veterans in news stories","https://doi.org/10.1177/0095327X18784238"]," shared on X. In analyzing 1,460 stories, we identified three themes, which together described a majority of stories: veterans as heroes, as recipients of charity, or as victims of mental or physical harm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some military veterans may be heroes, and some may face challenges related to trauma, reintegrating into civilian society or navigating government bureaucracy. Such coverage may certainly be newsworthy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem, ",["according to critics of veterans’ representation","https://doi.org/10.21061/jvs.v6i1.156"]," in news media, is that not much else appears in the media. As ",["one veteran told a researcher","https://doi.org/10.21061/jvs.v6i1.156"],", “It doesn’t sell newspapers that Joe Smith from Davenport went to Afghanistan three times, got out of the military, went to college, and now works as an account manager for American Eagle.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["But media representations of social groups shape our perceptions of the world. A 2021 experiment found that ",["exposure to stereotypical news stories","https://doi.org/10.1177/0095327X20986145"]," about veterans led readers to associate veterans with post-traumatic stress disorder, a ",["misunderstood and stigmatized condition","https://doi.org/10.1037/sah0000222"],". This, in turn, led readers to feel less desire to be socially close with veterans. The outcome illustrated how stories can have unintended downstream consequences even when journalists are covering newsworthy topics – in this case, PTSD and homelessness."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also tested whether reading a second story – one in which veterans talked about media stereotypes – would dampen those negative effects. It worked, illustrating the importance of a news feed that provides nuance."]},{"k":"p","s":["In another study, ",["we asked 1,047 U.S. adults","https://doi.org/10.21061/jvs.v6i3.207"]," to picture a veteran, describe the veteran and then explain where the image originated. When people depended on media for their image, rather than personal experience, they called to mind stereotypical images such as homelessness, PTSD and heroism."]},{"k":"p","s":["Given these stereotypes, a number of veterans organizations are advocating for broader, more insightful media representation. ",["Military Veterans in Journalism","https://www.mvj.network/"]," and ",["Veterans in Media & Entertainment","https://vmeconnect.org/"]," are nonprofits that help veterans pursue professional careers in news and entertainment media, motivated in part by the potential for veterans to produce nuanced stories about military life. There are also nonprofit news organizations, such as ",["The War Horse","https://thewarhorse.org/"],", seeking to bridge the military-civilian gap through storytelling and investigative reporting."]},{"k":"h","s":["Beyond ‘thank you’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Media can draw attention to veterans. Obama’s airport surprise ",["racked up 10.8 million views","https://x.com/BarackObama/status/1988230502197649568"],", 136,000 likes and 18,000 shares on X. But it will take more than made-for-media moments to bridge the military-civilian gap. That includes taking conversations with veterans offline."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a 2019 study, U.S. Air Force Maj. Nicholas J. Mercurio conducted focus groups with ",["veterans and active-duty service members","https://doi.org/10.21061/jvs.v4i2.103"]," and asked how they felt about “reflexive and formulaic expressions of gratitude” from the public such as “thank you for your service.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Responses were mixed, in part because veterans assumed civilians did not understand what that service entailed. Nonetheless, there was general agreement that civilians could go beyond thank you by showing interest in the personal experiences of veterans and having sincere conversations about their jobs."]},{"k":"p","s":["In doing so, civilians can demonstrate “interest in the individual,” Mercurio wrote, “not what they represent.”"]}],"chars":7039},"https://theconversation.com/queensland-nt-economic-growth-beats-the-rest-of-the-nation-led-by-mining-296503":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T05:33Z","sha":"476dfbd988eb5877d3b62ef7d9d4678f50c27ff79aa7283f9705e5761dd92b17","read":"https://theconversation.com/queensland-nt-economic-growth-beats-the-rest-of-the-nation-led-by-mining-296503","bytes":179556,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Queensland, NT economic growth beats the rest of the nation, led by mining","by":[{"n":"John Hawkins","r":"Senior lecturer, Canberra School of Government, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T04:28:49Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Coal production and oil and gas extraction helped Queensland and the Northern Territory economies grow faster than all the other states last year, new data show."]},{"k":"p","s":["Their growth was highlighted in annual data from the ",["Australian Bureau of Statistics","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/economy/national-accounts/australian-national-accounts-state-accounts/2025-26-financial-year"]," comparing economic performance across the Australian states."]},{"k":"p","s":["The report focuses on ",["gross state product (GSP)","https://www.abs.gov.au/methodologies/australian-national-accounts-state-accounts-methodology/2024-25-financial-year"],". This is the state and territory equivalent of ",["gross domestic product","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/economy/national-accounts/australian-national-accounts-national-income-expenditure-and-product/latest-release"]," (GDP), the most commonly used measure of the size of the national economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["The fastest growing were those with the largest mining sectors. The Northern Territory economy grew by 3.2% driven by strength in oil and gas extraction and gold mining. Queensland grew 3.1%, with mining the biggest contributor as well, led by increased coal production on rising export demand. Western Australia grew 2.4%."]},{"k":"p","s":["Victoria posted the slowest growth in the nation at just 1.7% in 2025-26."]},{"k":"p","s":["Across the nation, Australia’s total GDP grew by 2.3% in the year to June 2026. The ABS noted that growth was recorded across all industry groups. The largest contributors included finance, mining, construction and health care."]},{"k":"h","s":["The largest state economies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Unsurprisingly, New South Wales and Victoria, the most populous states, also have the largest sized economies overall. They account for 31% and 23% of our national economy. Queensland and Western Australia are catching up, now accounting for 19% and 16%."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ACT, with a ",["population","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/population/national-state-and-territory-population/latest-release"]," of 490,000, has a larger GSP than Tasmania – despite the Apple Isle’s bigger population of 581,000. A higher proportion of the ACT’s younger ",["population has a job","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/labour/employment-and-unemployment/labour-force-australia/latest-release"],". And the ",["more educated workforce","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/education/education-and-work-australia/latest-release#education-and-employment"]," is more productive."]},{"k":"p","s":["All states and territories expanded their economies in 2025-26."]},{"k":"p","s":["States whose populations are growing faster are likely to have faster growth in GSP."]},{"k":"p","s":["On a per person basis, the fastest growth was in the Northern Territory and Tasmania. Tasmania is not usually thought of as a mining state, but this year gold production made a significant contribution. The ",["farm sector","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/economy/national-accounts/australian-national-accounts-state-accounts/2025-26-financial-year#tasmania"]," also contributed with strong demand for meat and a good crop harvest."]},{"k":"p","s":["The weakest performer was Victoria where GSP per person was unchanged. It was held back by a contraction in oil and gas extraction, while the biggest source of growth was in financial services and insurance."]},{"k":"h","s":["How has Victoria’s economy been going over the medium term?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Victorian government has been criticised for its handling of the state economy. And today’s flat GSP per person numbers will probably amplify that, especially coming in the midst of an election campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 2014–15 (the start of the Andrews-Allan-Carroll governments) the ",["average growth in real GSP per person","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/economy/national-accounts/australian-national-accounts-state-accounts/2025-26-financial-year#data-downloads"]," has been 0.8% in Victoria. This is actually slightly better than the national average of 0.7% over the same 11-year period."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Victorian economy grew more slowly during the COVID era, reflecting longer lockdowns."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over the longer term, Victoria’s economy has been affected by the gradual decline in Australia’s manufacturing sector as a share of the economy. Manufacturing is disproportionately represented in Victoria."]},{"k":"p","s":["So it is possible to reach different conclusions about Victoria’s relative economic performance, depending on the time period chosen for the comparison."]},{"k":"h","s":["How income differs across the states"]},{"k":"p","s":["A similar pattern to GSP can be seen in the data on ",["real gross state income","https://www.abs.gov.au/methodologies/australian-national-accounts-state-accounts-methodology/2024-25-financial-year"]," per person. This also captures the impact of swings in the prices of exports and imports."]},{"k":"p","s":["The major industry where this is important is mining. This creates more volatility in the average incomes in Western Australia and the Northern Territory than in other parts of the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["The mining states have benefited from ",["higher commodity prices","https://www.rba.gov.au/statistics/frequency/commodity-prices/2026/icp-1026.html"]," since the turn of the century."]},{"k":"p","s":["Western Australia’s good fortune is shared by redistributing some of it to the other states and territories through the ",["carve-up of revenue","https://theconversation.com/the-controversial-gst-deal-with-the-states-is-under-review-there-are-better-alternatives-266054"]," from the Goods and Services Tax (GST)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The extent of this distribution has, however, been reduced by a ",["controversial deal","https://www.sauleslake.info/gst-distribution-western-australia-vs-productivity-commission/"]," developed by then Treasurer Scott Morrison in 2018. This gives all states in theory a guaranteed minimum share of the GST pool, regardless of their revenue. In practice, this gives WA much greater fiscal capacity because of its mining royalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["The special deal was agreed despite WA having been supported by the rest of Australia when it was poorer for most of the 20th century."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["The controversial GST deal with the states is under review. There are better alternatives","https://theconversation.com/the-controversial-gst-deal-with-the-states-is-under-review-there-are-better-alternatives-266054"]]}],"chars":4451},"https://theconversation.com/how-the-us-power-rivalry-with-russia-and-china-is-turning-outer-space-into-the-next-battlefront-293414":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T14:24Z","sha":"de83fce945fa57687e0f496ee996720da330f538de04e4b908d3a33b11231af6","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-the-us-power-rivalry-with-russia-and-china-is-turning-outer-space-into-the-next-battlefront-293414","bytes":189127,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How the US power rivalry with Russia and China is turning outer space into the next battlefront","by":[{"n":"Scott Shackelford","r":"Professor of Business Law and Ethics, Indiana University"},{"n":"Eytan Tepper","r":"Research Professor in Space Governance and Security, Indiana University"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T13:36:29Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["U.S. Air Force Secretary Troy Meink recently confirmed that ",["the United States has weapons deployed in Earth’s orbit","https://abcnews.com/Politics/air-force-secretary-acknowledges-us-weapons-space/story?id=136437923"],". To date, the ",["U.S. Space Force","https://www.spaceforce.mil/about-us/"],", the space service branch of the U.S. armed forces, has provided ",["relatively few details","https://www.spaceforce.mil/News/Article-Display/Article/4601219/secaf-announces-on-orbit-space-control-weapons/"]," about what these weapons are or what they can do except that they are what Meink called “on-orbit space control weapons.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Meink’s announcement is significant, but not necessarily because the U.S. is the first country to place weapons in orbit. For years, ",["the U.S., Russia and China have accused each other","https://www.clickorlando.com/news/space-news/2026/09/21/us-military-publicly-acknowledges-it-has-weapons-in-space/"]," of developing and testing such capabilities, although none has publicly acknowledged deploying space weapons – until now."]},{"k":"p","s":["We are ",["scholars of space law","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=YnVdvEYAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"]," and ",["governance","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=YtgRGx0AAAAJ&hl=en&oi=sra"],", and ",["our research illustrates","https://ostromworkshop.indiana.edu/research/space-governance/index.html"]," the challenges of uniting diverse groups to establish norms related to the use of resources, safety zones and conflict prevention in new domains such as space. Without better communication and deeper coordination between the world’s space powers, we could witness the beginning of a space arms race."]},{"k":"h","s":["Failed attempts to prevent a space arms race"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1981, the ",["United Nations added","https://www.unoosa.org/pdf/gares/ARES_39_59E.pdf"]," the Prevention of an Arms Race in Outer Space, known as ",["PAROS","https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3895439?ln=en"],", to its agenda."]},{"k":"p","s":["More than four decades of diplomatic efforts under PAROS have ",["produced meager results","https://scholarship.law.slu.edu/lj/vol70/iss2/8/"],", though there was a ",["United Nations agreement in 2024","https://www.swfound.org/publications-and-reports/multilateral-space-security-initiatives"]," that made progress on reducing threats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite many ",["countries’ proclamations supporting space arms control","https://scholarship.law.slu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2468&context=lj"],", no multilateral treaty banning weapons in space has been adopted. With ",["global arms control generally in retreat","https://thegsinsight.com/arms-control-in-retreat-how-populism-and-great-power-politics-are-rewriting-global-disarmament-norms/"],", and the apparent lack of political will among the three major space powers, efforts to control space weapons have reached an impasse."]},{"k":"p","s":["The question increasingly is not whether an arms race in space can be prevented, but how it will be managed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ambiguities allow weaponization"]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Outer Space Treaty of 1967","https://2009-2017.state.gov/t/isn/5181.htm"],", to which all major space powers are parties, is often described by scholars, practitioners and policymakers as the constitution of outer space."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Article IV of the treaty","https://2009-2017.state.gov/t/isn/5181.htm"]," remains the only legally binding international provision specifically regulating weapons in outer space. The article prohibits countries from placing nuclear weapons or other weapons of mass destruction in orbit around Earth. It also imposes a broader prohibition on military activities on the Moon and other celestial bodies, including establishing military bases, testing weapons and conducting military maneuvers."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the article does not prohibit conventional weapons in Earth’s orbit. That omission is significant. The treaty can be understood as ",["implicitly permitting what it does not prohibit","https://www.armscontrol.org/factsheets/outer-space-treaty-glance"],": the placement of such weapons in orbit."]},{"k":"p","s":["China has used these ambiguities as cover for its own space weaponization efforts. In a 2007 test, ",["China destroyed one of its own satellites","https://www.cfr.org/backgrounders/chinas-anti-satellite-test"]," while in orbit, and it has recently ",["deployed a mysterious space plane","https://www.space.com/space-exploration/launches-spacecraft/chinas-secretive-space-plane-caught-on-camera-in-incredible-new-photo-released-by-us-military"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["China, nonetheless, ",["reacted critically","https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/u-s-eyes-china-and-russia-as-pentagon-confirms-space-weapons-2e373e47"]," to the recent U.S. weapons announcement. In September 2026, it urged Washington to ",["stop expanding its military presence in space","https://www.nbcnews.com/world/asia/china-warns-us-space-weapons-fuel-arms-race-rcna598070"],". That same month, Russia renewed calls for ",["the demilitarization of outer space","https://www.reuters.com/business/aerospace-defense/russia-says-there-is-still-time-stop-an-arms-race-space-after-us-orbital-weapons-2026-09-16/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Both countries have long advocated stronger international restrictions on space weapons. Russia and China twice ",["jointly proposed a treaty","https://apnews.com/article/nuclear-arms-space-un-russia-us-japan-561ab8ae569afd7ee79789588ca34033"]," prohibiting ",["the placement of weapons in outer space","https://www.globaltimes.cn/page/202610/1372769.shtml"],". ",["The U.S. opposed the proposals","https://spacenews.com/41842us-dismisses-space-weapons-treaty-proposal-as-fundamentally-flawed/"]," in 2014, pointing to their failure to also cover important ground-based, anti-satellite weapons."]},{"k":"p","s":["But Russian and Chinese declarations in favor of keeping weapons out of space sit uneasily alongside their own activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2020, U.S. Space Command, part of the Defense Department, ",["accused Russia of testing a space-based anti-satellite weapon","https://www.npr.org/2020/07/23/894905696/u-s-space-force-accuses-russia-of-in-orbit-testing-of-anti-satellite-weapon"]," after an orbiting Russian satellite released a projectile. ",["Russia said the spacecraft","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/u-s-accuses-russia-of-testing-anti-satellite-weapon-in-space"]," was performing an inspection mission."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, the United States said Russia had launched another satellite, Cosmos 2576, which it assessed to be a “counter space” weapon ",["capable of attacking other satellites","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq55ww5j7e2o"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["China has similarly demonstrated increasingly sophisticated operations in orbit. Five Chinese spacecraft conducted satellite flybys in 2024, an exercise that ",["a senior U.S. Space Force officer later described","https://www.space.com/space-exploration/satellites/us-military-practices-orbital-dogfighting-in-1st-ever-live-fly-exercise-in-space"]," as practicing “dogfighting in space.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["None of this proves that every suspicious Russian or Chinese spacecraft is a weapon. Many technologies used for servicing, inspection and maneuvering around satellites are inherently dual-use. But it does put Moscow’s and Beijing’s calls to keep weapons out of space in perspective."]},{"k":"p","s":["It also illustrates the security threat now taking shape. Washington can point to Russian and Chinese activities to justify its own weapons. Moscow and Beijing can now point to acknowledged U.S. weapons to help justify their actions, which could result in a self-fulfilling prophecy."]},{"k":"h","s":["War in space"]},{"k":"p","s":["Space has been part of warfare for decades. The 1991 Gulf War has sometimes been called the first “space war” because of ",["the unprecedented role satellites played","https://media.defense.gov/2017/Dec/29/2001861991/-1/1/0/T_KELLY_CENTRALIZED_CONTOL_OF_SPACE.PDF"]," in navigation, communications, intelligence and targeting. But satellites primarily supported military operations taking place on the ground."]},{"k":"p","s":["That distinction has gradually eroded. NATO formally recognized space as ",["a military theater in 2019","https://www.nato.int/en/what-we-do/deterrence-and-defence/natos-approach-to-space"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia’s 2022 invasion of Ukraine then demonstrated something different, in which the very definition of a weapon was challenged."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hours before Russian troops crossed the border, ",["a cyberattack disrupted the U.S. satellite network Viasat","https://www.technologyreview.com/2022/05/10/1051973/russia-hack-viasat-satellite-ukraine-invasion/"],", in what was ",["dubbed by commentators","https://www.cigionline.org/publications/the-first-space-cyber-war-and-the-need-for-new-regimes-and-policies/"]," as the first “ ",["space-cyber war","https://www.cigionline.org/publications/the-first-space-cyber-war-and-the-need-for-new-regimes-and-policies/"],".” Space-based services were no longer merely supporting military operations but were themselves deliberately targeted as part of a military campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["The acknowledgment of weapons in orbit represents another step in that evolution. Space assets are transitioning from systems that primarily support warfare in other domains to systems that can be weapons, targets and participants in combat and are often replete with ",["vulnerabilities","https://www.lse.ac.uk/ideas/projects/space-policy/publications/cyberattacks-on-satellites"]," that could be exploited by an adversary."]},{"k":"p","s":["That does not mean future space warfare will resemble Star Wars dogfights or Starfleet armadas taking on Borg cubes. But the emerging battlefield is likely to be much more complicated. Satellites can be disrupted through jamming and spoofing, disabled through cyberattacks, approached or manipulated by other spacecraft, attacked from Earth or potentially attacked by weapons already in orbit."]},{"k":"p","s":["This makes the connection between space and cyberspace particularly important. A country seeking to neutralize an adversary’s satellites may have several options, ranging from a cyberattack or electronic interference to physically damaging it. At the same time, space-based critical infrastructure has never been more ",["vital","https://www.oecd.org/en/publications/the-space-economy-at-a-glance-2026_cbf9b240-en.html"]," to the functioning of the global economy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Military strategy therefore has to adapt not merely to warfare in space but to warfare across an increasingly interconnected ",["space-cyber nexus","https://digitalcommons.law.uga.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1617&context=glr"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["An arms race that must now be managed"]},{"k":"p","s":["The important question is no longer whether space will become militarized. It has been militarized for decades. Nor is it even whether states will develop weapons capable of affecting objects in space. Several already have done so."]},{"k":"p","s":["The new question is how nations manage a strategic environment in which weapons are openly deployed in orbit, satellites are increasingly being targeted, and attacks can move between the space and cyber domains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public acknowledgment may itself have strategic consequences."]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.S. Space Force argues that revealing the existence of its orbital weapons can strengthen deterrence by ",["making adversaries aware","https://www.space.com/space-exploration/satellites/us-space-force-says-it-operates-weapons-in-orbit-our-aim-is-deterrence"]," that it possesses capabilities with which to respond. But transparency can also accelerate competition."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia and China can now point to U.S. weapons to justify deploying their own. The same logic and its consequences ",["animated debates during the Cold War","https://thebulletin.org/2026/09/the-us-acknowledged-its-space-weapons-now-it-must-build-guardrails/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Forty-five years after the United Nations began debating the prevention of an arms race in outer space, that arms race increasingly looks less like something to prevent than something governments must learn to manage."]}],"chars":8027},"https://theconversation.com/a-westmoreland-county-easement-shows-how-landowners-can-protect-farmland-without-selling-it-292856":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T15:33Z","sha":"b027f7da671f0ddce7b8b2bd765bfc1d17572756b5e4d2763ea2da7e24d85877","read":"https://theconversation.com/a-westmoreland-county-easement-shows-how-landowners-can-protect-farmland-without-selling-it-292856","bytes":190316,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"A Westmoreland County easement shows how landowners can protect farmland without selling it","by":[{"n":"Andrew P. Morriss","r":"Professor of Law, Bush School & School of Law, Texas A&M University; Institute for Humane Studies"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T13:35:30Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Scott Tomlinson still owns the 35 acres in Ligonier Township in Westmoreland County, Pennsylvania, that his family has cared for over seven generations. But in July 2026, he ",["sold part of what it means to own them","https://triblive.com/local/westmoreland/ligonier-township-farmland-protected-for-generations/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For US$139,000, Tomlinson gave the Western Pennsylvania Conservancy ",["the right to enforce restrictions on how the land is used","https://triblive.com/local/westmoreland/ligonier-township-farmland-protected-for-generations/"],", TribLive reported. The restrictions ",["protect its farmland and woods from future development","https://triblive.com/local/westmoreland/ligonier-township-farmland-protected-for-generations/"]," in perpetuity."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to the report, the property is about 80% forest, with slopes that drain into a tributary of ",["Loyalhanna Creek","https://www.laurelhighlandstrouttrail.org/loyalhanna"],". It includes habitat for buffalo nut, a shrub the state lists as a ",["rare species of concern","https://weconservepa.org/blog/buffalo-nut-a-hemi-parasitic-shrub/"],", and farm soils the USDA classifies as “ ",["farmland of statewide importance","https://efotg.sc.egov.usda.gov/references/public/LA/Prime_and_other_Important_Farmland.html"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["That is how a conservation easement works: The land stays privately owned, but its owners agree to ",["limits on what they can do with it","https://texaslandtrustcouncil.org/about/what-is-a-conservation-easement/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such agreements let today’s landowners make conservation decisions that ",["bind future owners","https://library.weconservepa.org/guides/149-conservation-easements"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In more than two decades of ",["studying private land conservation","https://digitalrepository.unm.edu/nrj/vol44/iss2/14"],", I have found that deciding which rights to give up, how to pay for conservation and how to handle future changes can be complicated. My family has also spent roughly two years negotiating an easement on our own family’s ranch in Texas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dividing the rights of ownership"]},{"k":"p","s":["Think of land ownership as a bundle of sticks, with each stick representing a different property right. Within the limits of the law, ",["owners can build on the land, farm it, subdivide it and more","https://library.weconservepa.org/guides/19-conservation-easement"],". An easement separates particular rights from the rest of the bundle."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, an ",["access easement","https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/easement"]," gives someone else the right to cross your property. In a conservation easement, the landowner voluntarily gives up the right to use the land in specified ways. A land trust or government agency receives the ",["right to enforce","https://texaslandtrustcouncil.org/about/what-is-a-conservation-easement/"]," those limits."]},{"k":"p","s":["Imagine someone who owns a 1,000-acre farm that has long been in her family. Development is spreading into the surrounding countryside, and neighboring farms are being divided into smaller properties or subdivisions. She wants her land to stay largely intact. One stick in her bundle is the right to subdivide."]},{"k":"p","s":["A farmer who grants an easement might agree to limit ",["how many parcels future owners can carve out of the farm","https://www.pecva.org/land-conservation/conserving-your-land/conservation-easements/what-is-a-conservation-easement/"]," while still allowing farming. The farmer could still sell the property or pass it on, but whoever owns it next would also be ",["bound by the restrictions","https://library.weconservepa.org/guides/149-conservation-easements"],", because the farmer can’t sell rights the farmer no longer owns. Those future owners may have no intention of subdividing. But the farmer who signs the easement can’t know what their children, or someone who buys the farm a century from now, will want to do."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tomlinson’s worry – that land his family has cared for since the 1870s could be sold off for development once he’s gone – plays out against a broader shift in the county’s farm landscape. According to the USDA Census of Agriculture, Westmoreland County experienced ",["a 10% decline in the total number of farms","https://triblive.com/local/westmoreland/countys-ag-challenge-keeping-the-next-generation-on-the-farm/"]," between 2017 and 2022, dropping from 1,099 to 989 farms, even as total farmland fell only about 4%."]},{"k":"p","s":["Easements like Tomlinson’s are one way landowners have responded. The Western Pennsylvania Conservancy says it has ",["permanently protected","https://waterlandlife.org/wpc-conservation-easement-protects-more-farmland-and-forestland-in-westmoreland-county/"]," more than 30,000 acres in the Ligonier Valley since the 1970s, more than 12,000 of them through easements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Negotiating which rights to restrict"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Easement terms are negotiated","https://montanalandtrusts.org/faqs/"]," ",["property by property","https://www.nvct.org/conservation-easement"],". In my family’s negotiations, we have had to work out what we and future owners can still do with the ranch. We have agreed to limit where future buildings can go, to permanently restrict the use of certain pesticides and to prohibit new roads and stream crossings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other easements may allow different ",["agricultural, forestry or construction","https://www.pecva.org/land-conservation/conserving-your-land/conservation-easements/what-is-a-conservation-easement/"]," activities, depending on their terms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reaching agreement can be expensive. Natural Lands, a Pennsylvania land trust, lists ",["typical transaction costs","https://www.natlands.org/resources/for-landowners/conserve-your-land/"],". These include surveys, appraisals, environmental assessments, legal fees, title work and documentation of the property’s existing condition. The cost to negotiate my family’s easement has run well into six figures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Once an easement is signed, the holder is responsible for monitoring and enforcing it for as long as it lasts. Land trusts commonly ask landowners for ",["stewardship funding","https://landtrustalliance.org/resources/learn/topics/stewardship/stewardship-costs"]," to help pay for that future work."]},{"k":"p","s":["The land trust that holds our easement will work with whoever owns the land after us, not just with us, so choosing the ",["right partner","https://library.weconservepa.org/guides/122-co-holding-conservation-easements"]," was an important part of our decision."]},{"k":"h","s":["How conservation is financed"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beyond transaction costs, ",["granting an easement","https://landtrustalliance.org/blog/voluntary-private-land-conservation-101"]," usually lowers a property’s market value."]},{"k":"p","s":["To see how this works, imagine the hypothetical farm is worth $4 million with its development rights and $2 million once an easement sharply restricts subdividing it. (These figures are for illustration; how much an easement lowers a property’s value varies widely with its location, development potential and the restrictions involved.) Appraisers often value an easement by comparing a property’s value ",["before and after","https://www.irs.gov/publications/p561"]," it’s placed on the land. Here, the easement would be worth $2 million: the amount it cuts from the property’s value."]},{"k":"p","s":["To encourage landowners to grant easements, U.S. tax law allows a ",["charitable deduction","https://www.irs.gov/publications/p526"]," for donated easements that meet detailed requirements. Easements can also be sold."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Tomlinson’s case, ",["private foundation grants","https://triblive.com/local/westmoreland/ligonier-township-farmland-protected-for-generations/"]," paid for the conservancy’s purchase. Government programs offer another route: The ",["U.S. Department of Agriculture","https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/programs-initiatives/ale-agricultural-land-easements"]," helps eligible organizations, such as land trusts and state and local governments, to buy easements on farmland. These payments and tax benefits can help landowners absorb the drop in property value. For the public, buying or subsidizing easements can ",["protect more land per dollar than buying land outright","https://ideas.repec.org/p/ags/aaea14/177182.html"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tax benefits and tax abuse"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tax breaks tied to easements have also invited abuse."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Internal Revenue Service has identified ",["inflated appraisals and improperly large charitable deductions","https://www.irs.gov/charities-non-profits/conservation-easements"]," as recurring problems. A ",["2019 report","https://www.gao.gov/assets/710/701269.pdf"]," by the U.S. Government Accountability Office found that some promoters sold investors stakes in partnerships and similar entities that then donated easements at inflated values. When appraisals exaggerate a property’s development potential, ",["investors can claim deductions based on those inflated values","https://www.gao.gov/assets/710/701269.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Congress later ",["restricted deductions","https://www.irs.gov/irb/2024-30_IRB"]," for certain conservation contributions by partnerships and corporations. Courts have also ",["disallowed deductions and imposed penalties","https://www.irs.gov/charities-non-profits/conservation-easements"]," in abusive transactions."]},{"k":"h","s":["What it means to protect land forever"]},{"k":"p","s":["To qualify for the federal charitable deduction, a donated easement must ",["protect the land permanently","https://www.irs.gov/publications/p526"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Property scholar ",["Gerald Korngold","https://www.nyls.edu/faculty/gerald-korngold/"]," of New York Law School has argued that the ",["permanence","https://dc.law.utah.edu/ulr/vol2007/iss4/3/"]," that makes easements attractive also makes them hard to adjust and that ",["changing ecological conditions and competing community needs","https://www.nyuelj.org/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/24.1-Korngold_Final.pdf"]," can create reasons to revisit restrictions."]},{"k":"p","s":["In one case Korngold describes, a ",["conservation easement in Vermont","https://digitalcommons.nyls.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1013&context=rooftops_project"]," blocked the federal government from adding the land to a national wildlife refuge – a move every party supported – because federal rules require clear title."]},{"k":"p","s":["I have taught property law for decades and have written about the ",["challenges of private land conservation","https://digitalrepository.unm.edu/nrj/vol64/iss1/2/"]," for much of that time. These experiences taught me that an easement has to address two things: what to protect and what happens if circumstances change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Negotiating one for my family’s ranch made that, and the bundle of sticks metaphor, real for me. We had to write language setting the dimensions of the particular sticks my grandchildren will live with, under conditions none of us can predict."]},{"k":"p","s":["Done properly, a conservation easement leaves room for land use to adapt without undermining its conservation goals. It lets landowners like Tomlinson’s family and mine protect land while keeping it in private hands."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more of our stories about ",["Pittsburgh and Pennsylvania","https://theconversation.com/us/pittsburgh-news"],"."]}],"chars":7882},"https://theconversation.com/how-to-avoid-charger-rage-the-unwritten-rules-of-ev-charging-etiquette-293546":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T03:08Z","sha":"1a037aedc90be2c33c4c0157ab09575a2a1ceefdc9fffa10cbed5d28c765b182","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-to-avoid-charger-rage-the-unwritten-rules-of-ev-charging-etiquette-293546","bytes":178456,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How to avoid ‘charger rage’: the unwritten rules of EV charging etiquette","by":[{"n":"Milad Haghani","r":"Associate Professor and Principal Fellow in Urban Risk and Resilience, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T01:48:58Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s electric vehicle (EV) market is growing at ",["a remarkable pace","https://theconversation.com/australias-ev-sales-are-skyrocketing-our-charging-infrastructure-may-soon-struggle-to-keep-up-289403"],". In just the first six months of 2026, ",["almost 158,000 EVs were sold","https://www.commbank.com.au/articles/newsroom/2026/09/ev-sales-australia-sep-2026.html"],". That makes up 26% of all new car sales during the period, up from 12.1% a year earlier."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are now more than 600,000 on Australian roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public charging infrastructure is expanding, but keeping pace with this growth is a ",["challenge","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wxZqkRncKiI"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["recent international comparison","https://www.tradingplatforms.io/reports/ev-charging-deserts/"]," of 46 countries ranked Australia seventh highest for the number of EVs per public charging point (around 39 vehicles per charger)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means more drivers are sharing a limited number of chargers, waiting for others to finish, and negotiating who gets to charge next. The pressure can become particularly notable ",["during busy travel periods","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-04-10/ev-chargers-needed-to-keep-up-with-surge-in-ev-sales-in-nsw/106545294"],", sometimes leading to ",["frustration","https://youtube.com/shorts/3dYu4Mzdpuw?si=tbhKTaIIWl6VxO83"]," and ",["disputes","https://insideevs.com/news/459558/video-tesla-senry-mode-owner-physically-attacked/"]," described as “ ",["charger rage","https://doi.org/10.1080/10304312.2025.2536516"],"”."]},{"k":"h","s":["The unwritten rules of public charging"]},{"k":"p","s":["Filling up at a petrol station is usually quick, and most of us are familiar with the unwritten rules. EV charging takes longer and the rules of sharing chargers are less established."]},{"k":"p","s":["So, how can we make the experience smoother for everyone? Here are some tips:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Know your place in the queue. At petrol stations, cars usually line up behind pumps, making it obvious who’s next. However, EV charging stations can be different, with several bays and waiting vehicles scattered around the site. If all chargers are occupied, identify who is already waiting and establish your place in the queue. Don’t assume being closest to a newly available charger gives you priority. A quick conversation can prevent misunderstandings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Move once you’ve finished charging. A charging bay is not an ordinary parking space. Leaving your car plugged in after charging finishes prevents someone else from using the charger. Monitor your charging progress and return promptly, particularly when others are waiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["Think about how much charge you need. EV charging ",["gets slower","https://exploren.com.au/ev-not-charging-the-same-speed-from-0-100/"]," as the battery approaches full capacity. When others are waiting and you haven’t yet reached 100%, consider whether you have enough charge to reach your destination or next charging stop."]},{"k":"p","s":["Communicate rather than assume. Another driver might have an urgent journey or need only a short top-up. A polite conversation can help resolve competing needs."]},{"k":"h","s":["What does the research tell us?"]},{"k":"p","s":["A recent ",["Dutch study","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tbs.2026.101290"]," asked 246 EV drivers an open-eneded question about what they considered appropriate behaviour at public chargers. Researchers grouped their responses into 11 different behaviours, with one mentioned far more frequently than the others: moving your vehicle once it has sufficiently charged."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, even this seemingly straightforward expectation came with qualifications. Some respondents considered it reasonable to leave a vehicle connected overnight, rather than having to move it in the middle of the night."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another ",["Dutch study","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tbs.2023.100572"]," – combining a survey of 313 EV drivers with an analysis of 2.1 million charging sessions in Amsterdam – found most drivers were happy to move their vehicles once charging was complete to make chargers available to others."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, the actual behaviour of drivers was more complicated. Among more than 736,000 charging sessions involving frequent local users, only 16.2% of drivers disconnected their vehicles within an hour of charging finishing. The rest took longer than an hour to disconnect."]},{"k":"p","s":["The researchers found drivers were particularly unlikely to disconnect in the evening or overnight."]},{"k":"p","s":["This shows how even widely recognised expectations can be difficult to follow in practice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Can charging etiquette be encouraged or enforced?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Charging providers are already introducing measures to discourage drivers from unnecessarily occupying chargers, a behaviour researchers call “charging hogging”."]},{"k":"p","s":["One approach is ",["idle fees","https://youtube.com/shorts/qoozPdRLqQA?si=tJat_6xUQ9h4ZOU7"],". These are additional charges imposed when a vehicle remains connected after charging has finished, usually following a short grace period."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Australia, ",["Chargefox","https://support.chargefox.com/hc/en-au/articles/7103154366223-Overstay-and-idle-fees"],", for example, applies these fees at selected charging stations. Drivers receive a notification when charging finishes, followed by a per-minute fee if they fail to move their vehicle after the grace period."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Tesla","https://www.tesla.com/support/charging/supercharger/fees"]," goes further at busy Superchargers. Its congestion fees can apply not only after charging finishes, but also once a vehicle reaches a specified battery level, commonly 80%. This discourages drivers from occupying a charger for the increasingly slow final stages of charging."]},{"k":"p","s":["But financial penalties are not the only option."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["2024 experiment","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cstp.2023.101143"]," involving 703 Dutch EV drivers tested different notifications intended to encourage drivers to move their vehicles after charging."]},{"k":"p","s":["Among fully electric vehicle drivers, offering an alternative reserved parking space increased the predicted probability of intending to move by 17%. A message reminding drivers of the social expectation to make chargers available to others increased it by 16%. Loyalty rewards also helped, though to a lesser extent."]},{"k":"h","s":["What now?"]},{"k":"p","s":["As EV ownership grows, charging etiquette will increasingly become part of everyday motoring."]},{"k":"p","s":["The research suggests we don’t necessarily lack ideas about what considerate charging looks like. The greater challenge is turning those expectations into shared conventions that drivers consistently follow."]},{"k":"p","s":["And those conventions cannot be identical everywhere. What is reasonable at a busy highway fast charger may be quite different from an on-street charger used overnight."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, expanding charging infrastructure is only part of the challenge. Learning how to share it matters, too."]}],"chars":5516},"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-ben-carroll-has-elevated-integrity-in-his-campaign-after-passing-it-by-in-2023-296273":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T07:28Z","sha":"150b8abebcb0c43336479b074420dcd7ad1bed04a6d9f2775229df29aa4a9793","read":"https://theconversation.com/view-from-the-hill-ben-carroll-has-elevated-integrity-in-his-campaign-after-passing-it-by-in-2023-296273","bytes":174213,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"View from The Hill: Ben Carroll has elevated integrity in his campaign after passing it by in 2023","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T06:06:09Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Victoria’s premier, Ben Carroll, has run one of the most unusual election campaigns in memory."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s not just that he’s trying to make a virtue out of confessing the mistakes of a government of which he was a leading player. That can be seen as born of desperation. It’s that he chose deliberately to have Labor offer a penance that has probably increased its self-harm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll knows that, on all the evidence, the state government is headed on Saturday for a massive trouncing, in which he could lose his own seat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Presumably he was also aware his decision to establish the royal commission into the Big Build would not necessarily help limit the government’s losses, and might hurt them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll admittedly needed to announce a royal commission as part of sharply differentiating himself from his predecessors. To maintain the resistance by Jacinta Allan was untenable. But he could have made the commission a promise, rather than having it start hearing evidence immediately."]},{"k":"p","s":["The evidence that has come out has reinforced everything that had been said about the Andrews-Allan administrations – it has been devastating for the state government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet Carroll took this course on timing regardless. We can’t see into his mind but on face value, he deserves a big tick for standing up for integrity."]},{"k":"p","s":["He said in an interview in The Australian this week that the royal commission would be “the thing that defines me”."]},{"k":"p","s":["But something else will define Carroll, more negatively. In 2023, when Dan Andrews stepped down, Carroll nominated to contest the ballot against Allan. But then he withdrew, and in return he became deputy premier."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carroll, in his interview with The Australian, was asked about whether a ballot would have given Labor MPs and members a chance for a debate on where he and Allan wanted to take the party and the state. He said:“I reflect on that often […]. But I can’t look back. I’ve got to look forward. And believe it or not, I believe I was meant to get the leadership, and you know if it came later than it was meant to be, that was it.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["In a left-dominated state caucus Carroll, from the right, would not have won. But if he had been defeated and gone to the backbench, he might have fought to change the government’s direction and perhaps may have wrested the leadership earlier."]},{"k":"p","s":["Importantly, he would have extricated himself from the tentacles of a government whose lack of integrity has been demonstrated beyond dispute."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the very least, he would have been seen as a man of principle."]},{"k":"p","s":["But whether for reasons of self-interest (becoming deputy premier), a calculation of the numbers (which he didn’t have) or a lack of courage, Carroll bypassed what would have been the brave path of integrity."]},{"k":"p","s":["It was a choice he may have been seeking to atone for in how robustly he framed his action on the royal commission."]}],"chars":2818},"https://theconversation.com/i-diagnose-human-cruelty-australian-and-nz-medical-workers-on-treating-palestinians-in-gaza-293222":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-24T20:53Z","sha":"91fb1a8de62292f23341ddb3c7d21db50921b48e01f56cfb406fd71dd9e1446e","read":"https://theconversation.com/i-diagnose-human-cruelty-australian-and-nz-medical-workers-on-treating-palestinians-in-gaza-293222","bytes":191006,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘I diagnose human cruelty’: Australian and NZ medical workers on treating Palestinians in Gaza","by":[{"n":"Martin Kear","r":"Lecturer, Department of Government and International Relations, University of Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-24T19:10:38Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":[["The Weight of Witness","https://publishing.hardiegrant.com/en-au/books/the-weight-of-witness-by-bushra-othman/9781764324434"]," joins a growing list of testimonies that contest the official narrative of the war in Gaza and its aftermath. Edited and introduced by a Palestinian–Australian surgeon, Bushara Othman, it brings together the stories of Australian and New Zealand health professionals who went to Gaza to provide medical treatment to Palestinians."]},{"k":"p","s":["Othman, a medical mission coordinator with the Palestinian Australian and New Zealand Medical Association, was the first Australian Palestinian woman – and Muslim woman – to volunteer as a doctor in Gaza. She completed three tours there."]},{"k":"p","s":["Review: The Weight of Witness, edited and introduced by Dr Bushara Othman (Readers and Writers Against the Genocide)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The book’s collection of firsthand accounts paints a vivid and morally confronting picture. Its stories show what it’s like to treat the thousands of wounded Palestinians who daily flood into the hospitals and treatment centres scattered throughout the Gaza Strip."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wajdi Hadi, a Sydney-based specialist anaesthetist, recalls of his time at Al-Shifa Hospital:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Suddenly the hospital was flooded with casualties. There were bodies and injured patients everywhere. Blood covered the floors. The scale of suffering was overwhelming."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Gaza War began with Hamas’ surprise attacks against Israel on October 7 2023, ",["which killed","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/7/three-years-of-israels-genocide-in-gaza-in-numbers"]," 1,139 Israelis, with another 240 taken prisoner. In the devastating response by Israel’s military since, ",["the UN estimates","https://cdn.vev.design/private/YAiRnRybi6Nly1kycpKMfCHes9D3/g685-unrwa-situation-report-238-on-the-humanitarian-crisis-in-the-occupied-palestinian-territory.pdf"]," approximately 74,500 Palestinians have been killed and a further 175,800 wounded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reports by an ",["independent United Nations commission","https://www.un.org/unispal/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/a-hrc-60-crp-3.pdf"],", ",["Human Rights Watch","https://www.hrw.org/sites/default/files/media_2024/12/gaza1224web.pdf"],", ",["Amnesty International","https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/mde15/8668/2024/en/"],", and the Israeli human rights organisation ",["B’Tselem","https://www.btselem.org/sites/default/files/publications/202507_our_genocide_eng.pdf"]," concur the Palestinians in Gaza have become victims of genocide, war crimes and crimes against humanity, perpetrated by the Israeli government and military."]},{"k":"p","s":["Under the UN Genocide Convention of 1948, genocide is ",["defined","https://www.un.org/en/genocide-prevention/definition"]," any of five acts “committed with intent to destroy, in whole or in part, a national, ethnical, racial or religious group”."]},{"k":"p","s":["This book reveals the anatomy of these crimes. It exposes the Israeli military’s intentional targeting of both medical facilities and practitioners throughout the Gaza Strip, in contravention of international law. And it shows how it sought to destroy the ability of Palestinians and international aid organisations to treat these wounded. By doing so, the military precipitated the disintegration of Palestinian society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Deliberate policies enacted by Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Remembering her time in Gaza, critical care nurse Cass Lillis observes:"]},{"k":"p","s":["What I witnessed in Gaza was not accidental. It was not inevitable. It is the result of deliberate policies enacted by Israel that have destroyed infrastructure, health care and the conditions required for life."]},{"k":"p","s":["Just as importantly, these accounts raise serious questions about the complicity of Western democracies, including Australia, in these crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["“We need our government to stand by Palestinians,” declares Perth-based nurse and Médecins Sans Frontières emergency coordinator Claire Manera."]},{"k":"p","s":["We need aid to be delivered safely to the population, at scale, and we need an end to the genocide. But most of all, we need Australia to stop manufacturing the parts of weapons that are supporting this genocide."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite the tragedy of the war, displayed so powerfully in these accounts, the reader is occasionally provided with glimpses of humanity. These sit alongside a strong sense of Palestinians’ determination to survive this catastrophe – and to refuse to submit to Israeli efforts to erase them as individuals and as a people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Overall, the book is a testament to its contributors, all medical staff. It allows them to record their experiences of treating victims of a genocide, and the devastating effects this has on them – physically, mentally and morally."]},{"k":"p","s":["As Othman writes,"]},{"k":"p","s":["The antidote to grief is action, and I felt it both a moral necessity and a professional duty to report back on the crimes Israel had committed, and to highlight the honour and dignity of Gaza and its people."]},{"k":"h","s":["Screams from wounded children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Modher Albeiruti, an Iraqi–Australian emergency consultant, says life in Gaza removes the distance between observer and participant."]},{"k":"p","s":["He travelled to Gaza as a volunteer with the Palestinian American Medical Association for two weeks. But he was one of 16 international doctors and medical workers ",["stranded inside a hospital","https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/21/australian-doctor-modher-albeiruti-trapped-gaza-hospital-khan-younis-rafah"]," after Israel took control of the Palestinian side of the Rafah border crossing in May 2024. He ",["was evacuated","https://www.illawarramercury.com.au/story/8638077/dr-modher-albeiruti-evacuated-from-gaza-war-zone-to-jordan/"]," later that month."]},{"k":"p","s":["Scarlett Wong, a clinical psychologist and member of Médecins Sans Frontières, gave a speech to Australia’s Parliament about her experiences in August. She tells of colleagues who now enter Gaza with the calories of any food items they bring counted by the Israeli military, in case they decide to share their food with Palestinians."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Anything to sustain life is forbidden from being brought in: batteries, formula, medication,” she said. She goes further, declaring: “You want to know the diagnosis of mental health issues in Gaza: I diagnose human cruelty; I diagnose erasure; I diagnose genocide.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Other contributors speak of the stark contradictions between the perception and reality of the war for Palestinians as outsiders and witnesses. They regularly note the horrors they saw were far worse than they had imagined, or had seen portrayed by the Australian and international media."]},{"k":"p","s":["A regular theme is the devastating effects modern weapons and warfare have on the human body, especially on children. According to a 2026 ",["independent UN commission report","https://www.un.org/unispal/document/coi-report-23jun26/"],", at least 21,000 children have been killed since the outbreak of hostilities in October 2023, with a further 44,000 wounded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Remembering the child casualties, general and colorectal surgeon Sanjay Adusumilli recounts countless amputations, opening numerous chests, and performing endless intestinal resections."]},{"k":"p","s":["And Albeiruti relates the story of a ten-year-old boy refusing sedation during painful procedures. The boy declared: “I am strong. I am patient.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Raised in the United Kingdom and the son of Palestinian refugees, ",["Mohammed Mustafa","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-08-04/dr-mohammed-mustafa-trying-to-build-gaza-childrens-hospital/105585000"]," was a trainee emergency doctor from Perth when he first went to Gaza. He recalled hearing the screams from wounded children entering the emergency department of the European Hospital in Gaza, after a children’s playground had been struck by an Israeli drone."]},{"k":"h","s":["Witness to genocide"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perhaps most disturbing and revealing of all is the account by Sydney general surgeon Jamal Merei. He details the deliberate targeting of the genitals of young Palestinian boys and men by Israeli snipers."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the wounds were generally survivable, the lack of functioning testes will dramatically affect the fertility of the next generation of Palestinian men, he writes, “[erasing] their biological markers with a single gunshot to thwart their masculinity”. These actions would certainly qualify as genocide under ",["international law","https://treaties.un.org/doc/publication/unts/volume%2078/volume-78-i-1021-english.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Coming to terms with these accounts leaves us, as readers, with a sense of helplessness and futility. It also leaves us with a searing sense of anger at the world’s failure to do more to intervene as yet another genocide unfolds on our televisions and mobile phones."]},{"k":"p","s":["The accounts of these doctors and nurses serve as the weight of witness to genocide – and to their compassionate efforts to treat the thousands affected by this tragedy."]}],"chars":7348},"https://theconversation.com/jensen-huangs-controversial-return-to-nvidia-poses-the-question-whats-the-point-of-a-board-297386":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-25T03:22Z","sha":"011ac1a85fdce59157f001e2684142af92ff0f5b7af8ec1f65b008a5f071b70b","read":"https://theconversation.com/jensen-huangs-controversial-return-to-nvidia-poses-the-question-whats-the-point-of-a-board-297386","bytes":183520,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Jensen Huang’s controversial return to Nvidia poses the question – what’s the point of a board?","by":[{"n":"Anish Purkayastha","r":"Senior lecturer, University of Sydney"}],"pub":"2026-11-25T01:46:09Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["It’s hard to think of Nvidia without picturing Jensen Huang. Rarely seen without his ",["signature black leather jacket","https://www.scmp.com/tech/tech-war/article/3375539/jensen-huang-returns-nvidia-applause-staff-no-trademark-leather-jacket-sight"],", Huang has led chipmaker Nvidia since co-founding it in 1993, turning it into a central player in the artificial intelligence (AI) boom."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier this month, Huang ",["resigned","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000082/nvidiaannouncesceotransiti.htm"]," as president, chief executive officer and a member of Nvidia’s board, in the wake of a ",["bombshell scandal","https://theconversation.com/why-is-nvidia-so-powerful-in-the-ai-world-and-what-could-jensen-huangs-scandal-really-cost-296257"]," involving affairs and alleged corporate espionage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Days later, the board ",["linked his departure","https://www.npr.org/2026/11/17/nx-s1-6044213/jensen-huang-nvidia-congress"]," to “personal behavior inconsistent with the company’s code of conduct, standards and cultural norms”. It ",["said","https://www.nhpr.org/2026-11-17/nvidia-board-says-it-does-not-intend-to-reinstate-jensen-huang-as-ceo"]," it did “not intend to reinstate” him."]},{"k":"p","s":["This week, however, it ",["voted unanimously","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000090/nov23pressrelease.htm"]," to bring him back, following a remarkable intervention by US President Donald Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many analysts have already weighed in on ",["why the US government intervened","https://theconversation.com/trump-had-4-reasons-to-convince-nvidia-to-rehire-jensen-huang-heres-why-it-matters-globally-297377"],". But there’s a deeper, more fundamental question here about corporate power."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a chief executive is seen as too valuable to lose, can a company’s board still hold them to account? If it can’t, what exactly is the board for?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Trump had 4 reasons to ‘convince’ Nvidia to rehire Jensen Huang. Here’s why it matters globally","https://theconversation.com/trump-had-4-reasons-to-convince-nvidia-to-rehire-jensen-huang-heres-why-it-matters-globally-297377"]]},{"k":"h","s":["The ‘key person risk’"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sometimes, the “ ",["hero","https://hbr.org/2021/05/the-myth-of-the-ceo-hero"],"” leader of a company can become its biggest vulnerability. In corporate governance, this is called “key person risk”. It is the danger a company comes to depend so heavily on one person that losing them would do serious damage."]},{"k":"p","s":["This problem often grows out of success. A founder who builds a business and shapes its culture becomes its public face. Staff, customers and investors start to see the person and the company as one."]},{"k":"p","s":["Think of Steve Jobs, co-founder and longtime chief executive of Apple, or even the fictional media magnate Logan Roy in the TV series ",["Succession","https://theconversation.com/celebrity-money-and-power-tvs-obsession-with-the-murdoch-family-dynasty-146113"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia itself recognised this risk before Huang’s brief removal. Its ",["2026 annual report","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000021/nvda-20260125.htm"]," warned the company was “highly dependent on the services” of its longstanding executive team, and that failing “to ensure effective succession planning, transfer of knowledge, and smooth transitions” could hinder its success in the long term."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite this, when Huang left, no permanent successor was ready. Nvidia’s chief financial officer, Colette Kress, ",["stepped in temporarily","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000082/nvidiaannouncesceotransiti.htm"]," while the board searched for a replacement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who’s watching the boss?"]},{"k":"p","s":["So, what is a board actually for? Shareholders can’t supervise the managers in a large company like Nvidia; instead, they elect a board of directors to do it for them. While the board isn’t involved in daily operations of the company, it approves big decisions, watches the chief executive and, if needed, replaces them."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s designed to solve something economists call the “ ",["principal-agent problem","https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-405X(76)90026-X"],"”. A company’s managers (the agents) may put their own interests ahead of the owners’ (the principals)."]},{"k":"p","s":["That’s why independence matters. Independent directors don’t work for the company and have no close financial or personal ties to its management. Filling a board with the chief executive’s employees (such as other senior executives) and friends is like letting students mark their own exams."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nvidia’s U-turn shows how fragile independence can be. A committee of independent directors is still ",["investigating","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000090/nov23pressrelease.htm"]," claims that Huang was targeted by China’s top spy agency."]},{"k":"p","s":["Huang is also ",["due to answer questions","https://www.axios.com/2026/11/17/nvidia-jensen-huang-congress-testify-dates"]," from US lawmakers behind closed doors on December 1. The board brought him back before either had finished."]},{"k":"p","s":["The board acknowledged that its decision to rehire Huang was heavily influenced by the US government. It ",["said","https://nvidianews.nvidia.com/news/nvidia-board-reinstates-jensen-huang-as-president-ceo-and-board-director"]," it was “confident” Huang posed “no national security risk”, based on “input from senior US government levels”."]},{"k":"p","s":["We have seen other boards cave under pressure before. In November 2023, OpenAI’s board fired its chief executive, Sam Altman. Within days, nearly all of its 770 staff ",["threatened to quit","https://www.pbs.org/newshour/nation/sam-altman-reinstated-as-openai-ceo-with-new-board-replacing-the-one-which-fired-him"],". Altman returned, and the board that sacked him was replaced."]},{"k":"h","s":["Independent of whom?"]},{"k":"p","s":["On paper, there are strong safeguards to protect board independence. For example, the Nasdaq stock exchange, where Nvidia is listed, ",["requires most directors to be independent","https://listingcenter.nasdaq.com/rulebook/nasdaq/rules/nasdaq-5600-series"],". The committees that check a company’s accounts and set executive pay must be fully independent."]},{"k":"p","s":["But these rules fall short in three ways."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, the board itself gets to decide who counts as “independent”."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, a US court ",["found","https://www.gibsondunn.com/delaware-chancery-court-invalidates-elon-musk-55-8-billion-equity-compensation-package/"]," several Tesla directors who approved Elon Musk’s pay deal were too close to him to be independent. A higher court later ",["restored the deal","https://www.gibsondunn.com/delaware-reinstates-musk-pay-package-slashes-345-million-fee-award/"]," on other grounds."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, directors get much of their information from the very executive team they are meant to be keeping in check."]},{"k":"p","s":["And third, a board without its own independent leader often struggles to push back against a chief executive. Nvidia only ",["appointed","https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581026000082/nvidiaannouncesceotransiti.htm"]," its first-ever board chair on the day Huang resigned."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why no one should be irreplaceable"]},{"k":"p","s":["“Key person” risk can’t be removed, but it can be managed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Boards can train a credible successor, appoint an independent chair before a crisis hits, and finish investigations before deciding. They should also explain their reasoning in public."]},{"k":"p","s":["An independent board that isn’t able to fire and replace a chief executive is just a cheer squad – not the umpire it’s supposed to be."]},{"k":"p","s":["This matters well beyond Silicon Valley. Many retirement funds around the world own shares in Nvidia. For the sake of protecting millions of people’s long-term savings, retirement funds and others representing shareholders should be advocating for better governance than we’ve seen at Nvidia so far."]}],"chars":5473},"https://theconversation.com/from-beau-lamarre-condon-to-erin-patterson-the-domestic-and-family-violence-we-dont-name-297619":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T07:38Z","sha":"335aa6b6a8c062324efda6dda471be6485242e84681ff33d037019bf0046f12c","read":"https://theconversation.com/from-beau-lamarre-condon-to-erin-patterson-the-domestic-and-family-violence-we-dont-name-297619","bytes":182445,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"From Beau Lamarre-Condon to Erin Patterson: the domestic and family violence we don’t name","by":[{"n":"Xanthe Weston","r":"Associate Professor of Domestic and Family Violence, Queensland Centre for Domestic and Family Violence Research, CQUniversity Australia"},{"n":"Raquel Peel","r":"Relationships Expert & Psychology Educator at the Queensland Centre for Domestic and Family Violence Research, CQUniversity Australia"},{"n":"Rebecca Wilcoxson","r":"Lecturer in Forensic Psychology, CQUniversity Australia"}],"pub":"2026-11-27T05:53:23Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":[["This week","https://theconversation.com/beau-lamarre-condon-has-been-found-guilty-of-two-murders-legal-experts-explain-why-296148"],", a New South Wales Supreme Court jury found former police officer Beau Lamarre-Condon guilty of murdering Jesse Baird and Luke Davies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The unanimous verdict – reached in just two hours – rejected his claim that he killed Baird in self-defence. Lamarre-Condon’s legal team are ",["yet to say","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-26/nsw-beau-lamarre-murder-conviction-what-happens-next/107427328"]," if they will appeal the conviction."]},{"k":"p","s":["Baird had ended contact with Lamarre-Condon months before the killings in February 2024, following a short, non-exclusive relationship. The jury accepted that Lamarre-Condon then broke into Baird’s home and used his police-issue pistol to shoot him and his new partner, Luke Davies, through a bedroom door as Davies tried to call triple zero."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the coverage has described this as a “double murder”. It was."]},{"k":"p","s":["But, it was also a domestic homicide: separation, jealousy, a sense of entitlement to a former partner, and access to a firearm are among the ",["most well-recognised","https://www.mdpi.com/2076-3425/15/6/589"]," risk factors for intimate partner homicide."]},{"k":"p","s":["The only thing that sets this case apart is that it happened between two men. That matters, because it shows how narrow our picture of domestic violence can be."]},{"k":"h","s":["The effect on women"]},{"k":"p","s":["Let’s be clear from the outset: intimate partner violence is overwhelmingly gendered. It has been described as a ",["national crisis","https://www.pmc.gov.au/sites/default/files/resource/download/unlocking-the-prevention-potential-4.pdf"],", with one in four of Australian women and one in 14 of men experiencing it since the age of 15."]},{"k":"p","s":["Intimate partner homicide is the most common type of murder in Australia. In 2024–25, domestic homicide took the life of ",["one woman every 11 days","https://www.aihw.gov.au/family-domestic-and-sexual-violence/responses-and-outcomes/domestic-homicide"],", and one man every 26 days. Separation, as in Jesse Baird’s case, is a time of heightened risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most of this violence is perpetrated by men against women, and children are harmed too, both directly and by living with it. So, it makes sense that our laws, services, and public campaigns focus on male violence against female partners. Decades of feminist advocacy built that response, and it saves lives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nothing here argues for diverting attention or funding from women and children. But a framework built around one type of victim can leave others outside it."]},{"k":"h","s":["Violence in LGBTQIA+ relationships"]},{"k":"p","s":["LGBTQIA+ people experience ",["higher rates","https://www.aihw.gov.au/family-domestic-and-sexual-violence/population-groups/lgbtiqa-people"]," of intimate partner and family violence than other Australians . ",["Some research suggests","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/15248380251361063"]," their rates are as high or higher than those of cisgender heterosexual women."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["Private Lives 3","https://www.latrobe.edu.au/arcshs/documents/arcshs-research-publications/Private-Lives-3.pdf"],", the largest survey of its kind in Australia, 41.7% of LGBTQIA+ respondents said they had experienced intimate partner violence. When the survey asked about specific behaviours, such as financial and emotional abuse, that figure rose to 61%."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["meta-analysis","https://doaj.org/article/36db8e663f954890894995641539fe48"]," specifically looking at men who have sex with men pooled 52 studies with about 32,000 participants. About 33% had experienced intimate partner violence, and about 29% reported using it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["LGBTQ+ people are being ignored in the national discussion on family and sexual violence","https://theconversation.com/lgbtq-people-are-being-ignored-in-the-national-discussion-on-family-and-sexual-violence-167634"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Emotional abuse was the most common form (33% experienced, 41% used), then physical violence (17% and 12%) and sexual violence (9% and 4%)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the abuse reported among LGBTQIA+ people looks familiar: control, isolation, threats, physical violence. ",["But there are distinct tactics too","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23271429/"],", such as threatening to “out” a partner to family, friends or an employer."]},{"k":"p","s":["LGBTQIA+ victim-survivors also face real barriers to getting help. Many fear discrimination. Many services are designed and funded to support women escaping men’s violence, so a gay man or a woman abused by her female partner may not see a place for themselves. Some may not recognise what is happening to them as domestic violence at all."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lamarre-Condon case adds another layer. The perpetrator was a serving police officer, and he used his service weapon. For communities whose trust in police has ",["long been fragile","https://theconversation.com/the-policing-of-lgbtq-people-casts-a-long-dark-shadow-marching-at-mardi-gras-must-be-backed-up-with-real-change-224633"],", that matters. When the person you might report to looks like the person who hurt you, help can feel out of reach."]},{"k":"h","s":["When women are the offenders"]},{"k":"p","s":["The other case that belongs in this conversation is Erin Patterson."]},{"k":"p","s":["In July 2023, ",["she murdered","https://theconversation.com/four-victims-no-remorse-erin-patterson-given-a-life-sentence-for-mushroom-murders-264128"]," three members of her family: her parents-in-law, Don and Gail Patterson and her husband’s aunt, Heather Wilkinson. She also attempted to murder Ian Wilkinson."]},{"k":"p","s":["In October 2026, the Victorian Court of Appeal ",["dismissed her appeal","https://www.supremecourt.vic.gov.au/news/erin-patterson-appeal-judgments"]," and resentenced her to life in prison without parole. Her team has ",["since indicated","https://www.theage.com.au/national/victoria/erin-patterson-to-launch-high-court-appeal-in-last-ditch-bid-for-freedom-20261127-p61hua.html"]," they will try to appeal both her sentence and conviction in the High Court."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was family violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Patterson had separated from her husband, Simon, years earlier, and the victims were his family."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet across the investigation, the trial and the appeal, it has rarely been described that way. Instead it became the “mushroom murder”: a ",["true-crime puzzle","https://theconversation.com/a-shakespearean-small-town-murder-why-australia-became-so-obsessed-with-the-erin-patterson-mushroom-case-259982"],", a small-town tragedy, an international media spectacle."]},{"k":"p","s":["That framing is not accidental. Women who kill within their families are often treated as aberrations: mad, bad, or inexplicable. Their violence is seen as so far outside the norm that it doesn’t fit the categories we use for men."]},{"k":"p","s":["But women can be controlling, manipulative and violent, often in ways that are ",["less visible than men’s","https://theconversation.com/women-can-be-psychopaths-too-in-ways-more-subtle-but-just-as-dangerous-84200"],". When we fail to name their offending as family violence, we miss the patterns that come before it, and we overlook the people they harm."]},{"k":"h","s":["A bigger conversation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Lamarre-Condon and Patterson cases are very different, but they share a common thread: neither fits the picture most of us carry of domestic and family violence. That picture is accurate for most victims, but it isn’t complete."]},{"k":"p","s":["Naming violence accurately is the first step to preventing it. That means better data on LGBTQIA+ victims and on women who offend, services that are visibly inclusive, and risk assessment that focuses on the dynamics of a relationship rather than who is in it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women and children must remain at the heart of our response. But every victim deserves to be seen."]}],"chars":5768},"https://theconversation.com/how-the-uks-net-migration-figure-hit-its-target-after-years-of-government-promises-297787":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-27T18:25Z","sha":"d669869674999490f63dc2f30aae229a9c1d334cba4c86a0e684229381d89889","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-the-uks-net-migration-figure-hit-its-target-after-years-of-government-promises-297787","bytes":180391,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How the UK’s net migration figure hit its target after years of government promises","by":[{"n":"Ben Brindle","r":"Senior Researcher, Migration Observatory, University of Oxford"}],"pub":"2026-11-27T16:38:50Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In January 2010, ahead of the general election, then-prime minister David Cameron pledged to bring net migration down to the “tens of thousands” a year. Neither Cameron nor his successor, Theresa May, managed it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Net ",["migration","https://theconversation.com/topics/migration-412"]," – the number of people moving to the UK minus those leaving – averaged ",["around 250,000","https://ifs.org.uk/publications/migration-and-public-finance-forecast"]," during the 2010s. It never dropped below 100,000, except for a brief period during 2020 after COVID put a sudden stop to people moving around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["That was until the year ending June 2026, when net migration ",["fell to 77,000","https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/internationalmigration/bulletins/longterminternationalmigrationprovisional/yearendingjune2026"],". This was the lowest level (outside of the pandemic) ",["since 1997","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cq36gj12n0l3o"],". What makes the milestone particularly remarkable is that just three years ago, net migration stood at a historic ",["high of 944,000","https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/internationalmigration/bulletins/longterminternationalmigrationprovisional/yearendingjune2026"],". Since then, it has plummeted by 92%."]},{"k":"p","s":["So why have the numbers fallen, and are these low levels here to stay?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Fewer arrivals"]},{"k":"p","s":["The main reason for the decline is lower immigration into the UK. But understanding which government is responsible depends on the period you’re looking at."]},{"k":"p","s":["The previous Conservative government is largely responsible for both the increase and the initial decrease in net migration. Under Boris Johnson, it liberalised the immigration system after Brexit, reintroducing post-study work visas for international students, opening humanitarian routes for Ukrainians and Hong Kongers, and making care workers eligible for work visas."]},{"k":"p","s":["But as net migration reached record levels, Rishi Sunak’s government introduced a ",["suite of policies","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/home-secretary-unveils-plan-to-cut-net-migration"]," to restrict immigration. These included a ban on care workers and most international students bringing their family members, as well as increased scrutiny of applications to hire migrant care workers."]},{"k":"p","s":["The restrictions led to a sharp decline in immigration – but largely because immigration had been so high."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labour introduced further restrictions in 2025, most notably ",["closing the care route","https://www.gov.uk/government/news/overseas-recruitment-for-care-workers-to-end"]," to overseas workers. It also announced ",["tighter rules for universities","https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6821f334ced319d02c906103/restoring-control-over-the-immigration-system-web-optimised.pdf#page=39"]," sponsoring international students. This may have made institutions more cautious about offering places, even before the changes took effect in June this year."]},{"k":"p","s":["These changes have driven the decline over the past year, but have had a smaller impact because net migration was already much lower when Labour entered office."]},{"k":"p","s":["One reason recent government policies have been more effective at reducing immigration than those of the 2010s is that Brexit gave policymakers greater control over arrivals. Under free movement, EU citizens could move to the UK without a visa, limiting successive governments’ ability to restrict immigration from the bloc. Now, the government can restrict arrivals from any country, particularly those coming for work or study."]},{"k":"h","s":["More departures"]},{"k":"p","s":["Immigration is only one part of the story. High levels of emigration have also helped bring the net figure below 100,000. Much of this is a legacy of the post-pandemic boom, because many migrants – particularly students and workers – stay in the UK for only a few years. In other words, many of those who arrived during the recent period of record immigration are now leaving."]},{"k":"p","s":["EU citizens who arrived under free movement also contributed to the emigration figures."]},{"k":"p","s":["The previous government is therefore largely responsible for today’s high emigration figures. This is not because of its restrictive policies, but due to its more liberal policies a few years earlier."]},{"k":"p","s":["The number of UK citizens leaving the country has also attracted attention. Recent figures are substantially higher than those for the 2010s. But this is not the result of a sudden exodus – instead, in 2021 the ",["Office for National Statistics","https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/internationalmigration/articles/ukemigrationexplainedwhatweknowaboutbritsmovingabroad/2026-05-21"]," changed how it estimates British emigration. This has not only increased the emigration estimates, reducing the net migration figure by tens of thousands, but it also means comparisons with the 2010s are unreliable."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, some British emigrants may be people who originally moved to the UK from the EU under free movement and subsequently acquired UK citizenship. It is unclear how many people this applies to, however. Data from the UN show that between 2020 and 2024, ",["Poland, Malta and Romania","https://www.thetimes.com/uk/politics/article/exodus-uk-citizens-immigration-eastern-europe-w8563rpnv"]," saw the largest increases in their UK populations. Some may have also been joined by UK-born partners and children."]},{"k":"h","s":["Will net migration stay this low?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Looking ahead, low net migration will not necessarily represent a new normal. The UK is experiencing an unusual combination of falling immigration and relatively high emigration. This could even push net migration down further next year, as recent visa figures suggest immigration has further to fall."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the downward pressure from emigration is unlikely to last forever. Since fewer migrants are arriving, fewer will leave in the years ahead. As a result, emigration is likely to fall, which would push net migration back up even if immigration remains at its current level."]},{"k":"p","s":["After more than a decade of governments trying and failing to bring net migration down, the UK has finally reached ",["Cameron’s infamous target","https://www.compas.ox.ac.uk/article/long-read-curtains-at-last-for-the-net-migration-target"],". But some pretty specific circumstances have made that possible, and they will not all be in place forever."]}],"chars":5078},"https://theconversation.com/victoria-state-election-results-at-a-glance-296509":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-28T08:43Z","sha":"a8d1a2ee80a73f250b625b1cb28be75065192d31c2cad552da7883f366640f2b","read":"https://theconversation.com/victoria-state-election-results-at-a-glance-296509","bytes":170255,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Victoria state election: results at a glance","by":[{"n":"Digital Storytelling Team","r":"The Conversation"}],"pub":"2026-11-28T07:37:00Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Polls have closed across Victoria and the vote counting has begun. After ",["12 years in power","https://theconversation.com/victorias-12-year-labor-government-is-about-to-end-could-the-new-premier-kick-start-a-wider-liberal-party-redemption-296051"],", Labor is expected to lose the state election. It’s forecast the party could lose up to 30 seats in parliament."]},{"k":"p","s":["One Nation is looking to make its mark, and the rest of the country will be watching, although opinion polls have softened for the party over the course of the campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["It seems this is the Liberals’ election to lose."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep this page open, we’ll be projecting seats as the night goes on."]},{"k":"h","s":["How the Victoria election works"]}],"chars":518}};
